{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b6032e15baa6b787","type":"tool_result","content":"44\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega suite and spec conventions.\n45\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-error-wrapping-guide.md` — `github.com/bborbe/errors` API; never `fmt.Errorf`, never `context.Background()` inside `pkg/`.\n46\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100, `dupl`).\n47\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-patterns.md` — interface → constructor → struct, doc comments, error wrapping.\n48\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-security-linting.md` — gosec expectations.\n49\t\n50\t</context>\n51\t**Framework facts, all verified while writing this prompt against `github.com/bborbe/agent v0.89.0` at `$(go env GOMODCACHE)/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0`.** Read these files before writing code:\n52\t\n53\t- `agent_step.go` — `type Step interface { Name() string; ShouldRun(ctx, *Markdown) (bool, error); Run(ctx, *Markdown) (*Result, error) }`. A `Result` carries `Status AgentStatus`, `NextPhase string`, `Message string`. The framework marshals the mutated `*Markdown` after each step's `Run` and publishes it through the `ResultDeliverer`, so the `*Markdown` **is** the delivered body.\n54\t- `agent_markdown.go` — `type Markdown struct { Frontmatter TaskFrontmatter; Preamble string; Sections []Section }`, `type Section struct { Heading string; Body string }`, and `FindSection(heading string) (*Section, bool)`. `Sections` is an exported slice, so removal is a filter over it. There is **no** `RemoveSection` method.\n55\t- `agent_task-frontmatter.go` — `type TaskFrontmatter map[string]interface{}` with `func (f TaskFrontmatter) String(key string) (string, bool)`.\n56\t- `claude/agent-step.go` — `claude.NewAgentStep(claude.AgentStepConfig{Name, Runner, Instructions, EnvContext, OutputSection, NextPhase}) agentlib.Step`. On a `done` runner body it calls `md.ReplaceSection(Section{Heading: cfg.OutputSection, Body: <raw model response>})` and returns `Result{Status: AgentStatusDone, NextPhase: cfg.NextPhase}`. On a runner body that parses to a `needs_input` / `failed` envelope it returns that status **without writing the section**. On a runner error it returns `Result{Status: AgentStatusFailed, Message: \"<name> claude run failed: ...\"}`.\n57\t- `agent_agent.go` — `Agent.Run` walks phases in-process: after a step returns `Done` with a `NextPhase` that names another phase on the same `Agent`, the next phase runs in the same process. It exits on any non-`Done` status.\n58\t- `delivery/content-generator.go` — `NewPassthroughContentGenerator()` writes `## Failure` from `result.Message` for `failed` / `needs_input`, inside a ```` ``` ```` fence, and applies `status` / `phase` frontmatter. `agentlib.AgentResultInfo` is `{Status, Output, Message, NextPhase, ContinueToNext, AgentTurns, InteractionCount}`.\n59\t- `mocks/claude-claude-runner.go` — the counterfeiter fake is importable as `agentmocks \"github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks\"` and offers `RunReturns(result *claude.ClaudeResult, err error)`, `RunReturnsOnCall(i int, result *claude.ClaudeResult, err error)`, `RunCallCount() int` and `RunArgsForCall(i int) (context.Context, string)`. Use it for every step test.\n60\t- `github.com/bborbe/errors` — `errors.Errorf(ctx, format, args...)` produces an error whose `Error()` is exactly `fmt.Sprintf(format, args...)`; `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, format, args...)` wraps. Import as `\"github.com/bborbe/errors\"`.\n61\t\n62\t**Two facts verified empirically for this prompt:**\n63\t\n64\t1. `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` parses `file:line: pkg/x/y.go:42` with the key `file:line` and the value `pkg/x/y.go:42`, and parses a block scalar `confidence: |` + two indented lines into a value containing `\\n`. A block scalar value ends with a trailing newline, so the newline check must be `strings.Contains(v, \"\\n\")`.\n65\t2. `agentlib.ParseMarkdown` splits a body at every column-0 `## ` line. A `## Verdict` section whose body contains a column-0 `## Verdict` line therefore round-trips into two sections. This is exactly the forgery the heading rule must catch **before** the markdown is re-parsed, which is why the rule runs inside the step's `Run`.\n66\t\n67\t</context>\n68\t\n69\t<requirements>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"ebbd5964-7c68-4974-9f99-6635dc5922cb","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:25:28.964Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
