{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_4edc6ffc7c824052993be16d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three prompt files are written and structurally verified.\n\n## Files created\n\n- `/workspace/prompts/1-spec-002-verdict-gate.md` (474 lines) — model-output heading rule, verdict gate rules a–j, ai_review re-gate, line guard, stale-`## Failure` removal, all as step wrappers. Covers AC4–AC7.\n- `/workspace/prompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md` (261 lines) — `pkg/prompts/planning.md` / `execution.md` / `ai_review.md`, phase-aware `BuildInstructions`, deletion of `workflow.md`, three distinct factory steps. Covers AC8.\n- `/workspace/prompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md` (294 lines) — `agentDir` on the runner seam, gate wrapping, `defect-diagnose` in / `llm` out, the ten-case wired phase-chain test matrix, README mapping section, CHANGELOG. Covers AC2, AC3, AC9.\n\nExecution order is 1 → 2 → 3 (`make precommit` gates every one; AC1 is in each prompt's `<verification>`).\n\n## Key decisions\n\n1. **New package `pkg/verdict`** holds everything prompt 1 adds. Pinned exported API: `NewGate(envContext, cloneRoot) *Gate`, `(*Gate).Evaluate` (rules a–j), `(*Gate).Review` (rules a–j again, then the ai_review line guard), `CheckLineGuard`, `PrefixMessage`, and `NewPlanningStep` / `NewExecutionStep(inner, gate)` / `NewAIReviewStep(inner, gate)`. A follow-up prompt in the spec wires exactly these names.\n2. **`Gate` is a concrete struct, not an interface** — no counterfeiter fake, because every test drives the real deterministic gate and an interface would have no second implementation. Flagged as an open question.\n3. **Section removal is a filter over `md.Sections`**, never string surgery, and the gate itself performs it on every \"removed\" outcome. `Decision` therefore carries only `Status` + `Message`.\n4. **Prefixing happens exactly once, in the step wrapper**, so model-passthrough envelopes and gate-generated messages share one path. `Decision.Message` stays raw; `PrefixMessage` is the only prefixing step. This is what makes the `> `-form assertions land on the delivered message rather than on the gate.\n5. **`Evaluate` vs `Review`** splits rule k's meaning by phase: `Evaluate`'s `Done` = \"advance to ai_review\", `Review`'s `Done` = \"the line guard passed, complete\".\n6. **Prompt 2 changes the *body* of `CreateAgentFromRunner`** (three per-phase steps) so the repo stays compiling after `workflow.md` is deleted; **prompt 3 adds the parameter, the gate wrapping and the dispatch**. Flagged as an open question because it deviates from the spec's decomposition table.\n7. **Prompt 3 owns the only `## Unreleased` entry**; prompts 1 and 2 state explicitly that they must not add one, because AC9 greps for it.\n8. **AC10 is excluded** from every `<verification>` — mentioned once in prompt 3's `<context>` as the spec's operator rung, with no commands.\n9. **Pinned reason strings** for every rule (a table in prompt 1), so the tests assert them character for character instead of the executor inventing wording.\n10. **No git / docker / kubectl / dark-factory / operator-note blocks** anywhere in the verification or constraints — `.dark-factory.yaml` is `workflow: direct` with no `hideGit`, but `/workspace` has no `.git` at all, so all AC checks are grep- and `make`-based.\n\n## Verification work done before writing\n\n- Grepped `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0` for the real signatures used: `Step`, `Markdown`/`Section`/`FindSection`, `TaskFrontmatter.String`, `Agent.Run`'s in-process phase walk, `claude.NewAgentStep`'s `ReplaceSection` + envelope handling, `NewAgentProvider`'s error text, `TaskType` constants, `delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator`, and `mocks.ClaudeRunner`'s `RunReturns` / `RunReturnsOnCall` / `RunCallCount` / `RunArgsForCall`. No `defect-diagnose` constant exists upstream, so prompt 3 declares one locally.\n- Ran two throwaway programs to confirm load-bearing behaviour, then deleted them: `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` parses `file:line: pkg/x/y.go:42` with key `file:line`, and a block scalar yields a value containing `\\n`; `agentlib.ParseMarkdown` splits at every column-0 `## ` line (so an injected `## Verdict` becomes a second section — the exact forgery the heading rule must catch pre-parse); the passthrough generator splices `## Failure` from `result.Message` inside a fence.\n- **Reverted a `go.mod` side effect**: my scratch program promoted `gopkg.in/yaml.v3` from indirect to direct. It is back as `// indirect`; `go.sum` was untouched and the scratch directory is gone.\n\n## Open questions embedded as comments\n\n**Prompt 1** (7): pinned explicit messages for the section-missing / no-block / unparseable rows where AC4 says \"naming the field\" but no field exists; rule e deliberately does not echo the value (that is what makes AC4's `/abs/x.go:3`-absent assertion hold); the line guard quotes the **path** for `resolves outside the clone` / `not found in clone` but **path:line** for `beyond end of file`, read literally from the docs; AC5's \"each prefixed `> `\" is asserted at the delivered-message level because the prefix is applied once at the step boundary; the deepest-existing-ancestor walk is needed so a dangling directory escape still reports `resolves outside the clone`; the `service_repo.` literal is the lookup prefix, not a mapping entry, despite the Non-goal's wording; `Gate` is a concrete struct.\n\n**Prompt 2** (6): keeping the name `BuildInstructions` with a phase parameter rather than adding a second builder; a silent one-element fallback for an unknown phase instead of an error path through the factory; changing `CreateAgentFromRunner`'s body here rather than in prompt 3 (compile-green requirement); both planning and ai_review name `scripts/repo-clone.sh`, and all four names used are allowlisted so spec 001's consistency test needs no change; AC8's strings are asserted on `Instructions.String()`'s rendered form, which is what the model receives; `output-format.md` is kept and embedded for all three phases.\n\n**Prompt 3** (8): `CreateAgentFromRunner` gains `agentDir` because the clone root is unreachable through the `claude.ClaudeRunner` interface; AC3 is a factory-level matrix because only the real content generator produces \"the written task\"; the \"exactly two prompts\" assertions use `RunCallCount()`; the fixture sets `trigger_count: 1` / `max_triggers: 3` so the `failed` case keeps its assignee; the new tests construct `service_repo.<service>` keys in a local `envContext` — the only way to exercise rules h and i, and a direct tension with the Non-goal that the reviewer should confirm; README section placement is a readability choice; AC2's liveness assertion drives the liveness agent with the same fake; removing `llm` necessarily rewrites the accepted-types assertion to `[defect-diagnose healthcheck oauth-probe]`, which is read as excluded from \"all other existing tests keep passing\".\n\n## Docs referenced in `<context>`\n\nProject: `docs/verdict-gate.md`, `docs/observation-scripts.md`, `docs/dod.md`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `README.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `scenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md`, the two in-progress spec files, and the relocated spec-001 prompts (`prompts/completed/001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md`, `prompts/in-progress/002-…` and `003-…`).\nCoding plugin (in-container paths only): `go-testing-guide.md`, `go-error-wrapping-guide.md`, `go-precommit.md`, `go-patterns.md`, `go-security-linting.md`, `go-factory-pattern.md`, `go-doc-best-practices.md`, `changelog-guide.md`.\n\n## Pattern note\n\nNo reusable pattern was inlined that lacks a doc. One small suggestion: the Ginkgo suite-file boilerplate (`time.Local = time.UTC`, `format.TruncatedDiff = false`, 60 s suite timeout, `RunSpecs`) is now repeated across `pkg/scripts`, `pkg/factory`, `pkg/prompts` and `pkg/verdict`. Spec 001's prompt inlined it verbatim; these prompts reference `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go` as the shape instead. A short `go-ginkgo-suite-file.md` in the coding docs would remove the last reason to inline it.\n\nRun `/dark-factory:audit-prompt <file>` on each of the three before approving."}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash-max","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-878ead37275ea3cd","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"03495805-4d83-4db2-9b08-09b68facfa39","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:30:55.216Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-creator","task_description":"Generate prompts for spec 002"}
