{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab09421e009245fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tstatus: draft\n3\tspec: [002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate]\n4\tcreated: \"2026-09-28T01:40:00Z\"\n5\tbranch: dark-factory/diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate\n6\t---\n7\t\n8\t# Replace the scaffold prompt with one prompt per diagnoser phase\n9\t\n10\t<summary>\n11\t\n12\t- Each of the three diagnoser phases stops sharing one generic scaffold prompt and gets instructions written for that phase.\n13\t- Planning is told to resolve the observed service against the operator's mapping and to clone the mapped repo, and never to guess a repo.\n14\t- Execution is told which read-only scripts to call, in what order, and how to quote each call and its output as evidence.\n15\t- Review is told to re-check the verdict against the original observation, including whether the cited line supports the stated cause.\n16\t- Every phase is told never to start a line of its response with a hash sign, because the step supplies the heading.\n17\t- Every phase ends with the same JSON envelope the delivery layer already parses.\n18\t- The generic \"you are a task execution agent\" scaffold prompt is gone.\n19\t- The three phase steps are built in the factory with their own section heading and next phase, so the chain advances planning to execution to review to done.\n20\t- The instructions are embedded and checked by tests, so a phase prompt that loses a required instruction fails the build.\n21\t\n22\t</summary>\n23\t\n24\t<objective>\n25\t\n26\tGive each diagnoser phase instructions of its own. Today every phase shares one scaffold prompt that says nothing about defect diagnosis, so planning never resolves a service, execution never observes the running system, and review never checks the verdict. After this change `pkg/prompts/` carries `planning.md`, `execution.md` and `ai_review.md`, each embedded and selected by phase, and `pkg/factory` builds three distinct steps from them. The generic scaffold prompt is deleted, so no phase can fall back to it.\n27\t\n28\t</objective>\n29\t\n30\t<context>\n31\t\n32\tRead these before writing anything:\n33\t\n34\t- `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md` — read `## Desired Behavior` 2, 3 and 5, and `## Acceptance Criteria` AC8. AC8 pins the exact strings each phase prompt must contain.\n35\t- `docs/verdict-gate.md` — § The verdict block (the eight fields and their order, and the template you must copy into the execution prompt) and § Service → repo mapping input (the `service_repo.<service>` form the planning prompt must describe). Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\n36\t- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the authoritative contract for the four read-only scripts the prompts tell the model to call. The prompts must not contradict it, and must not invent a script.\n37\t- `specs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md` — the dependency spec. It provides the four scripts, the `GIT_REST_URL` / `PROMETHEUS_URL` forwarding and the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` string. **Spec 001 must be merged before this prompt runs.** Do not reimplement any of it, and do not edit `agent/scripts/`.\n38\t- `prompts/completed/001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` — house style for this repo.\n39\t- `prompts/in-progress/003-spec-001-config-allowlist-and-consistency.md` — the three-way consistency test that scans `pkg/prompts/*.md` for `scripts/<name>.sh` mentions and asserts each mentioned script is allowlisted. Every script name you write into a prompt must be one of the four allowlisted names, spelled exactly `scripts/vault-read.sh`, `scripts/vault-list.sh`, `scripts/prometheus-query.sh`, `scripts/repo-clone.sh`.\n40\t- `pkg/prompts/prompts.go`, `pkg/prompts/workflow.md`, `pkg/prompts/output-format.md`, `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go`, `pkg/prompts/prompts_suite_test.go` — the files this prompt changes.\n41\t- `pkg/factory/factory.go` — `CreateAgentFromRunner` builds the steps; read it before changing it.\n42\t- `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the guardrails prose the model reads alongside these prompts. Do not edit it; make the prompts consistent with it.\n43\t- `docs/dod.md` — the Definition of Done for this repo.\n44\t- `/home/node/.claude/CLAUDE.md` — the container's execution rules.\n45\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-testing-guide.md` — Ginkgo/Gomega suite and spec conventions, including `DescribeTable` / `Entry`.\n46\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-precommit.md` — linter limits that apply to test files too (`funlen` 80 lines / 50 statements, `gocognit` 20, `nestif` 4, golines max-len 100, `dupl`).\n47\t- `/home/node/.claude/plugins/marketplaces/coding/docs/go-doc-best-practices.md` — GoDoc comments start with the name and are full sentences.\n48\t\n49\t**Verified facts about the current code, read while writing this prompt:**\n50\t\n51\t- `pkg/prompts/prompts.go` embeds `workflow.md` and `output-format.md` and exposes `func BuildInstructions() claudelib.Instructions` returning a two-element `claudelib.Instructions` (`type Instructions []Instruction`, `type Instruction struct { Name, Content string }`). `claudelib.Instructions.String()` renders each element as `<name>content</name>` joined by newlines, and `claude.BuildPrompt(instructions, envContext, taskContent)` appends `## Environment` (the `ENV_CONTEXT` pairs, sorted) and `## Task` (the marshaled task document).\n52\t- `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go` asserts exactly three things about the scaffold builder: two instructions, the first named `workflow`, the second named `output-format`. Spec 002's `## Constraints` says those length/name tests are **replaced** by per-phase assertions; every other existing test keeps passing.\n53\t- `pkg/factory/factory.go` currently builds **one** `claude.NewAgentStep` with `OutputSection: \"## Result\"`, `NextPhase: \"done\"`, and registers it under `planning`, `domain.TaskPhaseExecution` and `ai_review`.\n54\t- `workflow.md` opens with `You are a task execution agent. Execute the task described below.` — the exact sentence AC8 forbids in any phase.\n55\t- `output-format.md` carries the frozen JSON envelope `{status, message, files}`. Keep it and keep embedding it for every phase.\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t<!-- Open questions for the reviewer — decisions taken here, each with the alternative:\n59\t\n60\t     1. The spec pins that the scaffold's BuildInstructions length/name tests are replaced\n61\t        by per-phase assertions, but it does not pin the builder's name or signature. This\n62\t        prompt keeps the name `BuildInstructions` and gives it a `domain.TaskPhase`\n63\t        parameter, so there is exactly one builder and no dead zero-arg one. Alternative: a\n64\t        new name (`BuildPhaseInstructions`) alongside the old, which leaves dead surface\n65\t        until prompt 3 deletes it.\n66\t\n67\t     2. The unknown-phase case returns a one-element Instructions (output-format only)\n68\t        instead of an error, because `CreateAgentFromRunner` has no error path and the\n69\t        factory only ever asks for the three canonical phases. Alternative: return\n70\t        `(claudelib.Instructions, error)` and change the seam's signature, which spreads an\n71\t        error path through two factory functions for a case that cannot occur.\n72\t\n73\t     3. This prompt changes the BODY of `CreateAgentFromRunner` even though the spec's\n74\t        Suggested Decomposition assigns factory work to prompt 3. Reason: deleting\n75\t        `workflow.md` and changing `BuildInstructions`'s signature leaves the repo\n76\t        non-compiling unless the single call site is updated in the same prompt, and every\n77\t        prompt must leave `make precommit` green. Reviewer: confirm the split — the body\n78\t        here, the signature change plus the gate wrapping plus the dispatch table in\n79\t        prompt 3.\n80\t\n81\t     4. Planning and ai_review both name `scripts/repo-clone.sh` (ai_review re-clones when\n82\t        the clone is absent). Spec 001's three-way consistency test requires every script\n83\t        named in `pkg/prompts/*.md` to be allowlisted, and all four names used here are in\n84\t        the allowlist, so no extra allowlist change is needed.\n85\t\n86\t     5. AC8 asserts the required strings on \"their built instructions\". `Instructions.String()`\n87\t        wraps each instruction in `<name>…</name>`, so the assertions are written against\n88\t        that rendered form — which is also exactly what the model receives through\n89\t        `claude.BuildPrompt`. Alternative: assert on the raw embedded `Content`, which would\n90\t        not cover the wrapping the model actually sees.\n91\t\n92\t     6. `output-format.md` is kept and embedded for all three phases, so the frozen JSON\n93\t        envelope still reaches every phase. AC8's \"no phase contains `You are a task\n94\t        execution agent`\" is satisfied by deleting `workflow.md`, not by editing it. -->\n95\t\n96\t</context>\n97\t\n98\t<requirements>\n99\t\n100\t1. **Create `pkg/prompts/planning.md`.** Plain markdown, no XML wrapper, no frontmatter — it is embedded verbatim as one `claudelib.Instruction`. It must contain the literal strings `scripts/repo-clone.sh` and `service_repo.`, and the literal sentence `Never start a line of your response with #.` It must instruct the model to:\n101\t\n102\t   - act as stage 1 of the defect lane, in its planning phase, and read the `## Observation` section of the task as the operator's report of a misbehaving service — it contains no diagnosis, and the model must not ask for one;\n103\t   - resolve the service named in `## Observation` **only** by an exact, case-sensitive match against the `service_repo.<service>` entries listed in the prompt's `## Environment` section. Say plainly that the mapping is operator-supplied, that the match is exact and case-sensitive, and that there is no fuzzy match, no fallback, and no repo from the model's own knowledge;\n104\t   - on a match, run `scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` and record in the `## Plan` section the four keys `service`, `repo`, `clone_path` and `head_sha`, taking `clone_path` and `head_sha` from the script's stdout;\n105\t   - on no match, or when the clone fails, return the JSON envelope with `\"status\":\"needs_input\"` naming the service it could not resolve or the clone error it saw, and **never** substitute a repo of its own choosing;\n106\t   - never start a line of its response with `#`, because the step supplies the `## Plan` heading;\n107\t   - end its response with the JSON envelope defined by `<output-format>`, and put nothing after it.\n108\t\n109\t2. **Create `pkg/prompts/execution.md`.** It must contain the literal strings `scripts/vault-read.sh`, `scripts/vault-list.sh` and `scripts/prometheus-query.sh`, all eight verdict field names (`defect_id`, `service`, `repo`, `file:line`, `root_cause`, `recommended_fix`, `evidence`, `confidence`), and the literal sentence `Never start a line of your response with #.` It must instruct the model to:\n110\t\n111\t   - observe the running system in this order: first the task files, through `scripts/vault-read.sh` and `scripts/vault-list.sh`; then metrics, through `scripts/prometheus-query.sh`. Say that these four read-only scripts are its only eyes on the running system, that they cannot write, and that it must not reach a cluster address directly;\n112\t   - localise the cause in the clone that planning left, using `Read`, `Grep` and `Glob`;\n113\t   - re-clone with `scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` first if the clone is absent (for example after a pod restart);\n114\t   - emit a fenced ```` ```yaml ```` block inside the `## Verdict` section, with the eight keys in the contract's order. Copy the template from `docs/verdict-gate.md` § The verdict block into the prompt verbatim, including the `file:line: <path>:<line>` line;\n115\t   - copy `defect_id` from the task's frontmatter, never invent one;\n116\t   - put the exact script call and its output into `evidence` — a verdict whose evidence does not name a live read is rejected by the binary;\n117\t   - give a cause that is supported only by reading source a `confidence` below `High`, and reserve `High` for a cause the live reads show;\n118\t   - when no line can be cited, return the JSON envelope with `\"status\":\"needs_input\"`, write no `## Verdict` section at all, and make the message list each script call it tried and what that call returned;\n119\t   - never start a line of its response with `#`, because the step supplies the `## Verdict` heading;\n120\t   - end its response with the JSON envelope defined by `<output-format>`, and put nothing after it.\n121\t\n122\t3. **Create `pkg/prompts/ai_review.md`.** It must contain the literal strings `## Observation` and `file:line`, and the literal sentence `Never start a line of your response with #.` It must instruct the model to:\n123\t\n124\t   - re-check the `## Verdict` the execution phase wrote against the task's `## Observation`, and to fail the check rather than wave it through;\n125\t   - check four things, naming each: the verdict's `service` matches the service named in `## Observation`; `root_cause` explains the observed symptom; `evidence` quotes a script call and its output; the content of the line cited by `file:line` supports `root_cause`;\n126\t   - re-clone with `scripts/repo-clone.sh clone <repo>` if the clone is absent, and record in the `## Review` section any `head_sha` difference from the `## Plan` section;\n127\t   - on a failed check, return the JSON envelope with `\"status\":\"needs_input\"` naming the check that failed;\n128\t   - on a passing check, write the `## Review` section and return `\"status\":\"done\"`;\n129\t   - never start a line of its response with `#`, because the step supplies the `## Review` heading;\n130\t   - end its response