{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9348b142ed4c0839","type":"tool_result","content":"=== pkg/prompts ===\ntotal 20\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  224 Sep 27 23:30 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  160 Sep 28 01:05 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  576 Sep 27 23:30 output-format.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  736 Sep 27 23:30 prompts.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  575 Sep 27 23:30 prompts_suite_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node  863 Sep 27 23:30 prompts_test.go\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 1179 Sep 27 23:30 workflow.md\n\n=== agent/.claude ===\ntotal 4\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node   96 Sep 28 01:27 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  128 Sep 28 01:04 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 node node 2418 Sep 28 01:27 CLAUDE.md\n\n=== docs/dod.md ===\n# Definition of Done\n\nAfter completing your implementation, review your own changes against each criterion below. These are quality checks you perform by inspecting your work — not commands to run (linting and tests already ran via `validationCommand`). Report any unmet criterion as a blocker.\n\n## Code Quality\n\n- Exported types, functions, and interfaces have doc comments\n- Error handling follows project conventions (no silently ignored errors)\n- No debug output (print statements, fmt.Printf) — use structured logging\n\n## Testing\n\n- New code has good test coverage (target >= 80%)\n- Changes to existing code have tests covering at least the changed behavior\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- If `make precommit` fails due to a dependency vulnerability with a known fix version, update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`) as part of your change\n- No `exclude` or `replace` directives in go.mod (break remote install)\n\n## Documentation\n\n- README.md is updated if the change affects usage, configuration, or setup\n- Documentation is updated if the change affects behavior described in docs/ (notably `docs/observation-scripts.md` and `docs/verdict-gate.md`)\n- When changing CLI args, config fields, env vars, or flags (add, rename, remove, change default), grep the entire repo and update all references in docs/, README.md, examples, and comments\n- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under `## Unreleased`\n- New or changed integration seam (per the dark-factory scenario-writing rules, \"When to Write a Scenario\") → scenario under `scenarios/` added or updated\n\n=== mocks/mocks.go ===\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage mocks\n\n=== pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go ===\n// Copyright (c) 2026 Benjamin Borbe All rights reserved.\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style\n// license that can be found in the LICENSE file.\n\npackage factory_test\n\nimport (\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/ginkgo/v2\"\n\t. \"github.com/onsi/gomega\"\n\t\"github.com/onsi/gomega/format\"\n)\n\nfunc TestSuite(t *testing.T) {\n\ttime.Local = time.UTC\n\tformat.TruncatedDiff = false\n\tRegisterFailHandler(Fail)\n\tsuiteConfig, reporterConfig := GinkgoConfiguration()\n\tsuiteConfig.Timeout = 60 * time.Second\n\tRunSpecs(t, \"Factory Suite\", suiteConfig, reporterConfig)\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28d6fdd9d31fe55","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"21a8412b-674d-463e-a04b-bc071067bdb4","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:31:54.682Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
