{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82b56f1b92d8f360","type":"tool_result","content":"=== vendor dir? ===\nno vendor/\n\n=== repo refs to 'llm' (excluding go.sum/vendor) ===\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:48:- The `llm` task-type alias. It is not in the Config's `taskTypes` and is dropped from the dispatch table.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:63:  - `Get(\"llm\")` returns an error containing `unknown task_type`.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:192:1. **Dispatch and phase chain.** `defect-diagnose` routes to the diagnoser. `healthcheck` and `oauth-probe` still route to the liveness agent. `llm` is no longer accepted. Each diagnoser phase has its own instructions in `pkg/prompts/*.md`, and the phases walk in-process as long as each one succeeds:\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:257:| LLM router rate-limits or times out (rate limiting) | Runner error → `failed`, assignee kept, retried by trigger count | `## Failure` `claude run failed` | Automatic; escalates at the cap |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:277:| 3 | Dispatch (`defect-diagnose` in, `llm` out); phase-chain wiring with the gate wrappers; a provider seam for a fake runner; wired phase-chain tests; README mapping section; CHANGELOG; AC9 greps (scenario 001 edits already applied) | 1, 2 (docs) | 2, 3, 9 | prompts 1, 2 |\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:9:# not the launch-agent template, whose registry / resources shape / LLM endpoint are stale.\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:44:    # LLM auth — fleet norm: stateless token via the in-cluster claude-code-router.\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:64:2. Common classes: transient infra (retry), missing script or env (preflight gap — see [[Fail-Fast Preflight for Tool-Dependent LLM Agents]]), service did not resolve to a repo (mapping gap — escalate, do not invent), defect not reproducible (expected `needs_input`)\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:13:- The old generic `llm` task type is no longer accepted, so a task can no longer reach a prompt that says nothing about diagnosis.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:25:Join the two halves this spec built. The verdict gate and the line guard exist as agent steps after prompt 1; the three per-phase prompts exist after prompt 2; nothing routes a `defect-diagnose` task to any of it. This prompt changes the dispatch table so `defect-diagnose` reaches the diagnoser and `llm` no longer does, extends the runner seam so the factory can build the gate against the clone root, wraps each phase step with its binary checks, proves the whole chain end to end with a fake model, and documents the operator-supplied mapping the diagnoser depends on.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:38:- `pkg/factory/factory_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_suite_test.go`, `pkg/factory/factory_kafka_topic_test.go` — the existing specs. `factory_test.go`'s dispatch specs assert the accepted-types list `[healthcheck llm oauth-probe]` and that `TaskTypeLLM` returns the domain agent; both change here.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:58:- `github.com/bborbe/agent` exports `TaskTypeLLM = \"llm\"`, `TaskTypeHealthcheck = \"healthcheck\"` and the deprecated alias `TaskTypeOAuthProbe = \"oauth-probe\"`. It does **not** export a `defect-diagnose` constant, so this prompt defines one locally in `pkg/factory`.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:108:     8. Removing `llm` changes `pkg/factory/factory_test.go`'s accepted-types assertion to\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:112:        drops `llm`. -->\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:162:   Then change `CreateAgentProvider` to build the diagnoser through the seam and to drop `llm` from the table:\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:264:# the dispatch table has the new task type and no longer accepts llm\npkg/factory/factory_test.go:85:\t\t\tExpect(err.Error()).To(ContainSubstring(\"[healthcheck llm oauth-probe]\"))\n\n=== repo refs to defect-diagnose ===\nREADME.md:3:**Stage 1 of the defect lane** ([[Defect Lane Task Chain]]). Takes a `task_type: defect-diagnose` task — the operator's `## Observation` of a misbehaving service, with no diagnosis attached — and writes a `## Verdict` with a root cause and a `file:line`, verified against the running system rather than inferred from source.\nREADME.md:14:1. Agent pipeline ([[task/controller]] → Kafka → [[task/executor]]) spawns a K8s Job with the `defect-diagnoser-agent` image.\nREADME.md:47:The `Config` CRD's `spec.env` map becomes pod env vars, which `main.go` consumes via struct tags. Generic example (see `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` for the real values):\nREADME.md:91:- Dev: <https://dev.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\nREADME.md:92:- Prod: <https://prod.quant.benjamin-borbe.de/admin/defect-diagnoser-agent/setloglevel/3>\nmain.go:5:// Command defect-diagnoser-agent is the canonical AI-heavy agent: one Claude\nmain.go:39:\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\nmain.go:115:\tglog.V(2).Infof(\"defect-diagnoser-agent started phase=%s\", a.Phase)\nNEXT-DIRECTIONS.md:1:# NEXT-DIRECTIONS — defect-diagnoser-agent\nNEXT-DIRECTIONS.md:8:- Config CRD rendered for dev (`k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`) — **not applied**\nNEXT-DIRECTIONS.md:9:- `taskTypes: [defect-diagnose, healthcheck]`\nNEXT-DIRECTIONS.md:20:- **Secret** `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-secret.yaml` — `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` (router token) via teamvault\nNEXT-DIRECTIONS.md:25:- **How**: platform change in `agent-task-executor` + CRD to accept a service account; then RBAC `defect-diagnoser` (get/list pods, pods/log, events, jobs, deployments — no secrets/configmaps/exec) and a `pod-logs.sh` script. RBAC is production-touching — operator-gated\ncmd/run-task/main.go:5:// Command run-task is the local-CLI entry point for defect-diagnoser-agent.\ncmd/run-task/main.go:28:\t\"github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/factory\"\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:19:The scaffolded `defect-diagnoser-agent` Config allowlists five scripts, and none of them exists. One (`pod-logs.sh`) cannot work at all, because the Config CRD has no `serviceAccountName` field and an agent Job therefore has no Kubernetes read access.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:87:  - `grep -nE '^\\s+CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"$' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns exactly 1 line. This is anchored so a value that exists only in a YAML comment does not pass.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:88:  - `grep -nE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 1 line.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:89:  - `grep -nE 'CLAUDE_ENV: .*PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 1 line.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:90:  - `grep -nE '^\\s+(GIT_REST_URL|PROMETHEUS_URL):' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` returns 0 lines (exit 1): the dead plain-env keys are gone.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:93:- [ ] **AC8** Allowlist, scripts and prose agree, checked by a test that parses `ALLOWED_TOOLS` from `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml`:\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:97:  - Exact string: `grep -c 'ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:\\*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:\\*)\"' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` prints `1`.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:98:  - Negative: `grep -ciE 'pod[- ]?logs' k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md README.md pkg/prompts/*.md` prints `:0` for every file and exits 1.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:120:  - `grep -c 'Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2'` returns at least 1 on each of `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` and `README.md`.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:134:  export CLAUDE_ENV=\"$(sed -nE 's/^[[:space:]]+CLAUDE_ENV: \"(.*)\"$/\\1/p' ../../k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml)\"\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:193:- `k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml` keeps its \"NOT APPLIED\" header. Only `ALLOWED_TOOLS`, the env keys and the path-3 comments change.\nspecs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md:206:| git-rest or Prometheus down / 5xx (external unavailability) | Script exits non-zero with the status on stderr | Model sees stderr; the diagnosis escalation names it | Operator restores the endpoint and re-assigns: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent` |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:10:- Turn the scaffolded agent into the real stage-1 defect diagnoser. A `defect-diagnose` task goes through planning, execution and ai_review, and ends with either a `## Verdict` that names a root cause and a `file:line`, or an honest escalation to the operator.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:18:The scaffold's dispatch rejects `defect-diagnose`, which is the only work task type in its own Config. Every phase runs the same generic prompt and jumps straight to `done`. Nothing turns an operator's observation into a diagnosis, so the operator still diagnoses every defect by hand. That is the largest single interaction cost the defect lane exists to remove (goal SC2 of \"An Observed Defect Reaches human_review Without Me\").\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:24:A `defect-diagnose` task file runs through planning, execution and ai_review inside one agent. It ends in exactly one of two states. A `failed` outcome retries under the existing trigger-count budget, and at the cap it too reaches state 2.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:56:\"Wired agent\" means the agent returned by the provider's `Get(ctx, \"defect-diagnose\")`, built with a fake Claude runner and the `service_repo.` mapping in its env context. \"Written task\" means the file that `CreateFileResultDeliverer` writes.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:60:  - `Get(\"defect-diagnose\")` returns the diagnoser: running it at `phase: planning` sends the fake runner a prompt containing `scripts/repo-clone.sh`.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:71:  - (e) **Malformed verdict (rule a).** The execution response contains no yaml block. The written task has `phase: execution`, the assignee kept (`defect-diagnoser-agent`), a `## Failure`, and **no `## Verdict`**.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:135:  - frontmatter `task_type: defect-diagnose`, `phase: planning`, `status: in_progress`, `assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent` and `defect_id: rung1-<date>`\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:175:  -task-file=/tmp/defect-diagnose-rung1.md \\\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:179:  -allowed-tools='<ALLOWED_TOOLS copied verbatim from k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml>' \\\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:184:  -v=2 2> /tmp/defect-diagnose-rung1.log\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:185:grep 'cmd.Env =' /tmp/defect-diagnose-rung1.log\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:188:Check AC10 (a) or (b) against `/tmp/defect-diagnose-rung1.md`. Then clean up with `chmod -R u+w agent/repos && rm -rf agent/repos`, and stop both port-forwards.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:192:1. **Dispatch and phase chain.** `defect-diagnose` routes to the diagnoser. `healthcheck` and `oauth-probe` still route to the liveness agent. `llm` is no longer accepted. Each diagnoser phase has its own instructions in `pkg/prompts/*.md`, and the phases walk in-process as long as each one succeeds:\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:248:| No read path shows the misbehaviour | Execution returns `needs_input` with no Verdict, listing each read and its result | `## Failure` text | Operator adds context to the task and re-assigns: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent` |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:252:| Cited line fails the line guard (file moved, line beyond EOF, symlink escape), after ai_review or inside rule j | `needs_input`; Verdict removed; evidence quoted in `## Failure`; task stays at `phase: ai_review` (or `execution` for rule j) | `## Failure` names the path and the file's line count | `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" phase execution`, then `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent` |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:253:| Clone fails (private repo, disk full) (external unavailability / resource exhaustion) | Planning returns `needs_input` with the script's stderr | `## Failure` contains `git clone failed` | Disk full: re-assign to get a fresh pod (`vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent`). Private repo: operator diagnoses by hand and records the result in the task |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:277:| 3 | Dispatch (`defect-diagnose` in, `llm` out); phase-chain wiring with the gate wrappers; a provider seam for a fake runner; wired phase-chain tests; README mapping section; CHANGELOG; AC9 greps (scenario 001 edits already applied) | 1, 2 (docs) | 2, 3, 9 | prompts 1, 2 |\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:284:A deployed agent would fail every `defect-diagnose` task with `unknown task_type`. The operator would keep diagnosing each observed defect by hand, which is exactly the cost goal SC2 exists to remove. The Sentry analyzer is no substitute: its schema, prompts and required Sentry token are Sentry-specific, and it has no live-observation path. Doing nothing is not acceptable while the goal stands.\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:1:# Config CRD instance for defect-diagnoser-agent — stage 1 of the defect lane\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:5:#   kubectlnukedev  -n dev  apply -f k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:14:  name: defect-diagnoser-agent\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:17:  assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:18:  image: docker.prod.nuke.benjamin-borbe.de:443/defect-diagnoser-agent:dev\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:22:  # The PriorityClass `defect-diagnoser-agent` does NOT exist yet — creating it is cluster-scoped and\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:24:  priorityClassName: defect-diagnoser-agent\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:26:  # task_type is the WORK SHAPE (defect-diagnose), not the repo name — per the page's contract.\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:28:    - defect-diagnose\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:54:  # Holds ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (router token) — teamvault-resolved, see k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-secret.yaml (not yet written).\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:55:  secretName: defect-diagnoser-agent\nk8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-config.yaml:58:  # ServiceAccount `defect-diagnoser` (get/list on pods, pods/log, events, jobs, deployments;\ndocs/claude-oauth-setup.md:3:The defect-diagnoser-agent runner uses Claude Code CLI which requires OAuth credentials.\ndocs/claude-oauth-setup.md:4:Credentials are stored on a PVC (`defect-diagnoser-agent`) mounted at `/home/claude/.claude`.\ndocs/claude-oauth-setup.md:8:- PVC `defect-diagnoser-agent` exists in the target namespace\ndocs/claude-oauth-setup.md:34:          \"claimName\": \"defect-diagnoser-agent\"\ndocs/claude-oauth-setup.md:88:          \"claimName\": \"defect-diagnoser-agent\"\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:6:- Agent `bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent` deployed to dev\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:7:- Config CRD applied: `kubectlnukedev -n dev get config.agent.benjamin-borbe.de defect-diagnoser-agent` shows it\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:21:   task_type: defect-diagnose\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:22:   assignee: defect-diagnoser-agent\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:43:   kubectlnukedev -n dev get pods | grep defect-diagnoser-agent\nscenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md:65:3. Re-trigger: `vault-cli task set \"<title>\" assignee defect-diagnoser-agent`\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:12:- A `defect-diagnose` task finally routes to the diagnoser instead of being rejected as an unknown task type.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:25:Join the two halves this spec built. The verdict gate and the line guard exist as agent steps after prompt 1; the three per-phase prompts exist after prompt 2; nothing routes a `defect-diagnose` task to any of it. This prompt changes the dispatch table so `defect-diagnose` reaches the diagnoser and `llm` no longer does, extends the runner seam so the factory can build the gate against the clone root, wraps each phase step with its binary checks, proves the whole chain end to end with a fake model, and documents the operator-supplied mapping the diagnoser depends on.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:55:- `pkg/factory/factory.go` declares `const servi