{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab777eeaa034cec4","type":"tool_result","content":"=== BuildInstructions references ===\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:234:- The scaffold's `BuildInstructions` length/name tests are replaced by per-phase assertions. All other existing tests keep passing.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:36:- `pkg/prompts/` — **prompt 2's deliverable**. `prompts.BuildInstructions(phase)` and the three `*.md` files must already exist. If they do not, see the sentinel rule in `<requirements>`.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:118:0. **Fail-loud sentinels for the cross-prompt boundary.** Before writing anything, confirm `pkg/verdict/gate.go`, `pkg/verdict/step.go`, `pkg/verdict/lineguard.go`, `pkg/prompts/planning.md`, `pkg/prompts/execution.md` and `pkg/prompts/ai_review.md` all exist and that `prompts.BuildInstructions` takes a phase argument. If `pkg/verdict/` is missing or does not export the names below, stop and report `\"status\":\"failed\"` with the message `verdict gate not yet deployed (prompt 1 of spec 002)`. If the per-phase prompts or the phase-taking `BuildInstructions` are missing, stop and report `\"status\":\"failed\"` with the message `per-phase prompts not yet deployed (prompt 2 of spec 002)`. Never report `needs_input` for either — a missing prerequisite is a broken ship order, not a question for the operator.\nprompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md:175:   The map has exactly three entries. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` must not appear anywhere in `pkg/factory/`. `healthcheck` and `oauth-probe` keep returning the same liveness agent instance. The liveness agent's prompt must contain none of the diagnoser's instructions — it is built from `healthcheck.NewClaudeStep`, not from `prompts.BuildInstructions`.\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:51:- `pkg/prompts/prompts.go` embeds `workflow.md` and `output-format.md` and exposes `func BuildInstructions() claudelib.Instructions` returning a two-element `claudelib.Instructions` (`type Instructions []Instruction`, `type Instruction struct { Name, Content string }`). `claudelib.Instructions.String()` renders each element as `<name>content</name>` joined by newlines, and `claude.BuildPrompt(instructions, envContext, taskContent)` appends `## Environment` (the `ENV_CONTEXT` pairs, sorted) and `## Task` (the marshaled task document).\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:60:     1. The spec pins that the scaffold's BuildInstructions length/name tests are replaced\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:62:        prompt keeps the name `BuildInstructions` and gives it a `domain.TaskPhase`\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:75:        `workflow.md` and changing `BuildInstructions`'s signature leaves the repo\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:147:   // BuildInstructions assembles the prompt for one diagnoser phase: that phase's\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:149:   func BuildInstructions(phase domain.TaskPhase) claudelib.Instructions\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:162:       Instructions:  prompts.BuildInstructions(domain.TaskPhasePlanning),\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:183:   Build the instructions with `prompts.BuildInstructions(phase)` and render them with `.String()`, then assert, as a `DescribeTable` with one `Entry` per phase (`domain.TaskPhasePlanning`, `domain.TaskPhaseExecution`, `domain.TaskPhaseAIReview`):\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:190:   Then add a `DescribeTable` over `prompts.BuildInstructions(domain.TaskPhase(\"bogus\"))` asserting the one-element fallback returns only the `output-format` instruction. Keep every `It`/`Entry` body short by passing the required strings as `Entry` arguments rather than writing one spec per phase.\npkg/prompts/prompts_test.go:14:var _ = Describe(\"BuildInstructions\", func() {\npkg/prompts/prompts_test.go:16:\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\npkg/prompts/prompts_test.go:21:\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\npkg/prompts/prompts_test.go:27:\t\tinstrs := prompts.BuildInstructions()\npkg/prompts/prompts.go:20:// BuildInstructions assembles the full agent prompt from embedded modules.\npkg/prompts/prompts.go:22:func BuildInstructions() claudelib.Instructions {\npkg/factory/factory.go:114:\t\tInstructions:  prompts.BuildInstructions(),\n=== NewAgentStep in factory ===\npkg/factory/factory.go:111:\tstep := claudelib.NewAgentStep(claudelib.AgentStepConfig{\n=== any service_repo in repo (non-prompt) ===\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:45:- A general service → repo mapping, or `service_repo.` entries in any Config or code file of this repo. The mapping is operator-supplied input (contract open question 4).\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:56:\"Wired agent\" means the agent returned by the provider's `Get(ctx, \"defect-diagnose\")`, built with a fake Claude runner and the `service_repo.` mapping in its env context. \"Written task\" means the file that `CreateFileResultDeliverer` writes.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:93:  - Service `Agent-Task-Controller` against mapping key `service_repo.agent-task-controller`: `needs_input` containing `does not resolve` (the match is exact and case-sensitive). No `## Verdict`.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:115:  - planning: contains `scripts/repo-clone.sh` and `service_repo.`\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:123:  - `grep -c 'service_repo\\.' README.md` is at least 1, and `grep -c 'docs/verdict-gate.md' README.md` is at least 1.\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:124:  - `grep -rn 'service_repo\\.' k8s/` returns 0 lines (exit 1).\nspecs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md:126:  - `sed -n '/^\\*\\*Setup\\*\\*/,/^\\*