{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7585dcd66021217","type":"tool_result","content":"=== assignee / previous_assignee in agent module (non-test) ===\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-frontmatter.go:38:func (f TaskFrontmatter) Assignee() TaskAssignee {\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-frontmatter.go:39:\tv, _ := f[\"assignee\"].(string)\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-frontmatter.go:40:\treturn TaskAssignee(v)\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:14:// TaskAssignee identifies which agent type handles this task.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:15:// Matched against Config CRD spec.assignee.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:16:type TaskAssignee string\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:18:func (t TaskAssignee) String() string {\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:22:func (t TaskAssignee) Validate(ctx context.Context) error {\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-assignee.go:24:\t\treturn errors.Wrap(ctx, validation.Error, \"assignee missing\")\n\n=== applyStatusFrontmatter ===\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/delivery/content-generator.go:52:func applyStatusFrontmatter(content string, result agentlib.AgentResultInfo) string {\nfunc applyStatusFrontmatter(content string, result agentlib.AgentResultInfo) string {\n\tswitch result.Status {\n\tcase agentlib.AgentStatusDone:\n\t\tif result.NextPhase == \"\" {\n\t\t\t// Done without NextPhase is an in-place save (see agentlib.Result.NextPhase:\n\t\t\t// \"Empty means stay in current phase\"): keep status: in_progress, preserve\n\t\t\t// phase from existing content. Terminating a task requires an explicit\n\t\t\t// NextPhase: \"done\".\n\t\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"status\", \"in_progress\")\n\t\t\t// phase intentionally not modified — preserves the current phase\n\t\t\tbreak\n\t\t}\n\t\tresolvedPhase := resolveNextPhase(\"\", result.NextPhase)\n\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"phase\", resolvedPhase)\n\t\t// Only mark the task completed when the resolved phase is terminal (done) —\n\t\t// mirrors the kafkaResultDeliverer frontmatter override.\n\t\tif resolvedPhase == \"done\" {\n\t\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"status\", \"completed\")\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"status\", \"in_progress\")\n\t\t}\n\tcase agentlib.AgentStatusNeedsInput:\n\t\t// task-level failure: agent ran cleanly but task is impossible/underspecified.\n\t\t// Clear assignee so the task surfaces in the operator inbox; record the pre-clear\n\t\t// owner (spec 027); preserve phase — human_review is reserved for Result.NextPhase.\n\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"status\", \"in_progress\")\n\t\tif prev := getFrontmatterField(content, \"assignee\"); prev != \"\" {\n\t\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"previous_assignee\", prev)\n\t\t}\n\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"assignee\", \"\")\n\t\t// phase is preserved from existing content — do NOT set to human_review\n\tcase agentlib.AgentStatusInProgress:\n\t\t// Step-level progress save: keep status: in_progress, preserve phase from incoming task.\n\t\t// Multi-step phase handlers use this to commit ## Plan / ## Result / etc. mid-phase\n\t\t// without triggering a phase transition.\n\t\tcontent = SetFrontmatterField(content, \"status\", \"in_progress\")\n\t\t// phase intentionally not modified — preserves the agent's current phase for in-place save\n\tcase agentlib.AgentStatusFailed:\n\t\t// Infra failure (transient — crash, timeout, OOM): preserve assignee so the task\n\t\t// stays routable and trigger_count / max_triggers retries can fire. At cap\n\t\t// exhaustion the task escalates to the operator inbox: assignee cleared,\n\n=== claude runner WorkingDirectory handling ===\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/agent-dir.go:15:// Resolve expands a leading \"~/\" to the user's home directory.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/agent-dir.go:16:// See ClaudeConfigDir.Resolve for full semantics.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/agent-dir.go:17:func (a AgentDir) Resolve(ctx context.Context) (string, error) {\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner-config.go:15:\t// WorkingDirectory sets the CLI process working directory.\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner-config.go:16:\tWorkingDirectory AgentDir\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner.go:122:\tresolved, err := cfgDir.Resolve(ctx)\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner.go:170:\tif r.config.WorkingDirectory != \"\" {\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner.go:171:\t\tworkDir, err := r.config.WorkingDirectory.Resolve(ctx)\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-runner.go:173:\t\t\treturn nil, errors.Wrap(ctx, err, \"resolve WorkingDirectory\")\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-config-dir.go:13:// Use Resolve when the path will cross into a subprocess or filesystem call —\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-config-dir.go:18:// Resolve expands a leading \"~/\" to the user's home directory. Empty input\n/home/node/go/pkg/mod/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0/claude/claude-config-dir.go:24:func (c ClaudeConfigDir) Resolve(ctx context.Context) (string, error) {","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cbee98593beadc5","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"0241e94e-20bf-4d6e-8773-58396723f8a1