{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-acb0d6ec1edeb826","type":"tool_result","content":"=== prompt 2 objective/requirements head ===\n---\nstatus: draft\nspec: [002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate]\ncreated: \"2026-09-28T01:40:00Z\"\nbranch: dark-factory/diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate\n---\n\n# Replace the scaffold prompt with one prompt per diagnoser phase\n\n<summary>\n\n- Each of the three diagnoser phases stops sharing one generic scaffold prompt and gets instructions written for that phase.\n- Planning is told to resolve the observed service against the operator's mapping and to clone the mapped repo, and never to guess a repo.\n- Execution is told which read-only scripts to call, in what order, and how to quote each call and its output as evidence.\n- Review is told to re-check the verdict against the original observation, including whether the cited line supports the stated cause.\n- Every phase is told never to start a line of its response with a hash sign, because the step supplies the heading.\n- Every phase ends with the same JSON envelope the delivery layer already parses.\n- The generic \"you are a task execution agent\" scaffold prompt is gone.\n- The three phase steps are built in the factory with their own section heading and next phase, so the chain advances planning to execution to review to done.\n- The instructions are embedded and checked by tests, so a phase prompt that loses a required instruction fails the build.\n\n</summary>\n\n<objective>\n\nGive each diagnoser phase instructions of its own. Today every phase shares one scaffold prompt that says nothing about defect diagnosis, so planning never resolves a service, execution never observes the running system, and review never checks the verdict. After this change `pkg/prompts/` carries `planning.md`, `execution.md` and `ai_review.md`, each embedded and selected by phase, and `pkg/factory` builds three distinct steps from them. The generic scaffold prompt is deleted, so no phase can fall back to it.\n\n</objective>\n\n<context>\n\nRead these before writing anything:\n\n- `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md` — read `## Desired Behavior` 2, 3 and 5, and `## Acceptance Criteria` AC8. AC8 pins the exact strings each phase prompt must contain.\n- `docs/verdict-gate.md` — § The verdict block (the eight fields and their order, and the template you must copy into the execution prompt) and § Service → repo mapping input (the `service_repo.<service>` form the planning prompt must describe). Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\n- `docs/observation-scripts.md` — the authoritative contract for the four read-only scripts the prompts tell the model to call. The prompts must not contradict it, and must not invent a script.\n- `specs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md` — the dependency spec. It provides the four scripts, the `GIT_REST_URL` / `PROMETHEUS_URL` forwarding and the `ALLOWED_TOOLS` string. **Spec 001 must be merged before this prompt runs.** Do not reimplement any of it, and do not edit `agent/scripts/`.\n- `prompts/completed/001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` — house style for this repo.\n- `prompts/in-progress/003-spec-001-config-allowlist-and-consistency.md` — the three-way consistency test that scans `pkg/prompts/*.md` for `scripts/<name>.sh` mentions and asserts each mentioned script is allowlisted. Every script name you write into a prompt must be one of the four allowlisted names, spelled exactly `scripts/vault-read.sh`, `scripts/vault-list.sh`, `scripts/prometheus-query.sh`, `scripts/repo-clone.sh`.\n- `pkg/prompts/prompts.go`, `pkg/prompts/workflow.md`, `pkg/prompts/output-format.md`, `pkg/prompts/prompts_test.go`, `pkg/prompts/prompts_suite_test.go` — the files this prompt changes.\n=== prompt 3 verification ===\n64:**AC10 (the rung-1 live run) is the spec's operator-executable rung.** It needs two port-forwards, the router token and a real dev service, so it cannot run inside this container. Do not attempt it and do not add it to `<verification>`.\n65-\n66-\n67-<!-- Open questions for the reviewer — decisions taken here, each with the alternative:\n68-\n69-     1. `CreateAgentFromRunner` gains a third parameter (`agentDir`) even though AC2 only\n70-        says the seam \"takes the runner\". The gate and the line guard need the clone root\n71-        (`<agent dir>/repos`), and nothing else on the seam can supply it: the\n72-        `claude.ClaudeRunner` interface exposes only `Run`, so the runner's working\n73-        directory is not readable from outside. Both call sites are inside `factory.go` and\n74-        are updated here; `CreateAgent`'s own signature — the one `cmd/run-task/main.go`\n75-        calls — is unchanged, and `factory_test.go`'s `CreateAgent` spec keeps compiling.\n76-\n77-     2. AC3 is implemented as ten specs in `pkg/factory/phase_chain_test.go` driving the\n78-        real provider and the real `CreateFileResultDeliverer`, rather than as more step\n79-        tests. AC3 asserts \"the written task\", which only the real content generator\n80-        produces (it is what applies `status` / `phase` and splices `## Failure`); the\n81-        step-level tables live in prompt 1.\n82-\n83-     3. AC3(b)(d)(e)(f) assert \"the fake runner captured exactly two prompts\". That is\n84-        implemented with `RunCallCount()` on the counterfeiter fake.\n85-\n86-     4. The task fixture sets `trigger_count: 1` and `max_triggers: 3`. Without a count\n87-        below the cap, the framework's `failed` path clears the assignee at cap exhaustion\n88-        and case (e) — which asserts the assignee is KEPT on `failed` — would fail for the\n89-        wrong reason.\n90-\n91-     5. The new tests construct `service_repo.<service>` keys in their own local\n92-        `envContext`. That is the only way to exercise gate rules h and i, and it is\n93-        simulated operator input rather than committed mapping data — consistent with the\n94-        spec's Non-goal and with AC9's `grep -rn 'service_repo\\.' k8s/` returning 0 lines.\n--\n226:9. **AC9 checks that need no edit, only confirmation.** `scenarios/001-diagnose-one-observed-defect.md` was already updated alongside this spec. Do not edit it. Confirm with the `<verification>` greps that its Setup block still carries a `service_repo.` entry and its Step 1 block still carries `defect_id`.\n227-\n228:10. **Self-check before finishing.** Re-run `<verification>` and confirm every line passes. Then walk AC2, AC3 and AC9 bullet by bullet against your change and confirm each is actually asserted — a case that asserts only the status and not the written task does not count. Confirm `cmd/run-task/main.go` and `main.go` still compile unchanged, and that the two `CreateAgentFromRunner` call sites are both updated.\n229-\n230-</requirements>\n231-\n232-<constraints>\n233-\n234-- **Contract** ([[Defect Lane Task Chain]], amended 2026-09-27; copied into `docs/verdict-gate.md` because the container cannot read the vault). Fixed: the `## Verdict` field names and their order; the `confidence` values `High | Medium | Low`; and the escalation split (no line → no Verdict; line + Medium/Low → Verdict kept; stage 2 only from High). `## Observation` is read and never rewritten.\n235-- **Gate rules are frozen in `docs/verdict-gate.md`.** Do not change that page, and do not change the rule behaviour prompt 1 shipped.\n236-- **Frozen envelope:** the final-response JSON `{status, message, files}` that the delivery layer parses is unchanged.\n237-- **Escalation mechanics are the framework's.** `needs_input` clears `assignee`, sets `previous_assignee` and writes `## Failure`. `failed` keeps the assignee for the trigger-count retry, and clears it only at cap exhaustion. Do not reimplement any of it.\n238-- **Phase cursor.** The diagnoser writes no frontmatter field of its own except `phase`. Prompt 1's step wrappers already set it on entry; do not add a second writer.\n239-- `healthcheck` / `oauth-probe` routing and the liveness agent are unchanged, and they share the one `runner` instance.\n240-- **Do NOT add a confidence-threshold knob and do NOT add a gate opt-out flag.** `High`-only is the contract; the spec's Non-goals forbid both outright.\n241-- **No committed mapping data.** No `service_repo.<service>` key/value pair may be hard-coded in the Config, in non-test Go code, or in any docs file. The README documents the **form** only. The new tests are the one exception and the reason the exception exists: they construct `service_repo.<service>` keys in their own local `envContext` to exercise rules h and i, which cannot be tested without them — that is simulated operator input, not committed mapping data.\n242-- **Do NOT add a `pod-logs.sh` or any pod-log / event read**, and do not re-introduce a pod-log mention into the README. That waits on the Config CRD gaining a service-account field and is an explicit spec Non-goal.\n243-- Do NOT change the `github.com/bborbe/agent` module or its version. No `go get`, no version bump, and never `-mod=vendor`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28d6fdd9d31fe55","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"d4bd5a66-95f6-4522-85e6-d0e0318f523d","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:36:24.281Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-958fe9270ea35a43","type":"tool_result","content":"=== completed 001 full frontmatter ===\n---\nstatus: completed\nspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\nsummary: Added three executable read-only HTTP observation scripts (agent/scripts/vault-read.sh, vault-list.sh, prometheus-query.sh) plus a subprocess-driven Ginkgo suite in pkg/scripts that drives them against a local recording server.\nexecution_id: defect-diagnoser-agent-diagnose-v1-exec-001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts\ndark-factory-version: dev\ncreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\nqueued: \"2026-09-27T23:01:28Z\"\nstarted: \"2026-09-27T23:01:29Z\"\ncompleted: \"2026-09-27T23:12:30Z\"\nbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n---\n\n# Add the three read-only HTTP observation scripts\n\n<summary>\n\n- The agent image gains three read-only helper scripts the model can call to read task files and metrics.\n- Reading one vault file and listing vault files both go through the vault's HTTP API with a GET only.\n- Querying Prometheus sends exactly one instant query to the fixed query endpoint and nothing else.\n=== 'verdict-gate.md' refs across prompts ===\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:34:- `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md` — read `## Desired Behavior` 2, 3 and 5, and `## Acceptance Criteria` AC8. AC8 pins the exact strings each phase prompt must contain.\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:35:- `docs/verdict-gate.md` — § The verdict block (the eight fields and their order, and the template you must copy into the execution prompt) and § Service → repo mapping input (the `service_repo.<service>` form the planning prompt must describe). Where it and any other source disagree, it wins.\nprompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md:114:   - emit a fenced ```` ```yaml ```` block inside the `## Verdict` section, with the eight keys in the contract's order. Copy the template from `