{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a6f8fe6ab36d9b0c","type":"tool_result","content":"=== agent dir ===\ntotal 0\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  128 Sep 28 01:04 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node 1184 Sep 28 01:32 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node   96 Sep 28 01:27 .claude\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 node node  192 Sep 28 01:17 scripts\n--- agent/repos? ---\nagent/repos does NOT exist\n\n=== .gitignore ===\n/.update-logs/\n/.claude/\n/CLAUDE.md\n/.mcp-*\n/run-task\n/cmd/run-task/run-task\n/vendor\n/.dark-factory.lock\n/.dark-factory.log\n/agent/repos/\n\n=== completed prompt 001 frontmatter ===\n---\nstatus: completed\nspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\nsummary: Added three executable read-only HTTP observation scripts (agent/scripts/vault-read.sh, vault-list.sh, prometheus-query.sh) plus a subprocess-driven Ginkgo suite in pkg/scripts that drives them against a local recording server.\nexecution_id: defect-diagnoser-agent-diagnose-v1-exec-001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts\ndark-factory-version: dev\ncreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\nqueued: \"2026-09-27T23:01:28Z\"\nstarted: \"2026-09-27T23:01:29Z\"\ncompleted: \"2026-09-27T23:12:30Z\"\nbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n---\n\n=== completed prompt 002 frontmatter ===\n---\nstatus: completed\nspec: [001-read-only-observation-toolkit]\nsummary: Added agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh, a read-only GitHub clone script with owner/name normalization, pre-git traversal and symlink containment guards, plus a stub-git Ginkgo suite, the /agent/repos/ gitignore line and a CHANGELOG entry\nexecution_id: defect-diagnoser-agent-diagnose-v1-exec-002-spec-001-repo-clone-script\ndark-factory-version: dev\ncreated: \"2026-09-27T22:45:00Z\"\nqueued: \"2026-09-27T23:02:59Z\"\nstarted: \"2026-09-27T23:12:31Z\"\ncompleted: \"2026-09-27T23:24:40Z\"\nbranch: dark-factory/read-only-observation-toolkit\n---\n\n=== verdict-gate.md mapping input section ===\n## Service → repo mapping input\n\nThe diagnoser owns no mapping data. The operator supplies entries through the existing `ENV_CONTEXT` channel, one per service:\n\n```\nENV_CONTEXT=service_repo.<service>=<owner>/<repo>,service_repo.<other>=<owner>/<repo>\n```\n\nThey render into the prompt's `## Environment` section as `service_repo.<service>: <owner>/<repo>`. A service resolves only on an **exact, case-sensitive** key match. No fuzzy match, no fallback, no repo from the model's own knowledge.\n\n## Model-output heading rule — applied in every phase, first\n\nAfter each model step reports `done`, and before any other check in that phase, the binary inspects the section the step just wrote:\n\n| Phase | Section checked |\n|---|---|\n| planning | `## Plan` |\n| execution | `## Verdict` |\n| ai_review | `## Review` |\n\nIf the section body contains **any column-0 line starting with `#`**, the phase yields `failed`. The message names the section (e.g. `heading rule: section \"## Plan\" contains a column-0 heading line`) and **never echoes the offending line**. No message the binary generates ever has a line starting with `#` (see § Failure messages). The offending section is removed from the task's parsed sections before delivery, so the written task never carries it.\n\nThis one rule covers every model-written section. It replaces the earlier per-section checks (verdict body, plan, review).\n\n**Why, and what is out of scope.** The root cause is a bborbe/agent framework defect: `Markdown.Marshal` writes model output verbatim, and the section splitter treats any column-0 `#` line as a heading while ignoring code fences. A model response containing a column-0 `## Verdict` line would otherwise become a second, forged section on the next parse. The defect is reported upstream, and fixing it is out of scope here. Inside this repo, heading injection is contained by four measures together:\n\n- this heading rule\n- § Failure messages (every `## Failure` line prefixed `> `, once)\n- § Echoed values\n- the read-only script allowlist\n\nEach phase's instructions also tell the model never to start a line of its response with `#`, because the step supplies the heading.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cbee98593beadc5","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"22ad6442-8eb4-4384-afce-39dde82866d1","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:37:16.528Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 3"}
