{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b9c6bcbf27186a4a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Creating Claude-Based Agents\n2\t\n3\tGuide for building new domain-specific agents on top of `agent/claude` as a copy-paste template.\n4\t\n5\t`agent/claude` is a **reference implementation** — a generic Pattern B agent (K8s Job spawned by `task/executor`) that wraps Claude Code CLI. It ships minimal so domain agents can fork it and swap:\n6\t\n7\t1. `.claude/CLAUDE.md` guardrails\n8\t2. `pkg/prompts/` (workflow + output format)\n9\t3. `ALLOWED_TOOLS` env\n10\t4. `scripts/` (safe shell APIs for domain I/O)\n11\t5. `main.go` struct fields for domain env (API URLs, credentials)\n12\t\n13\tNo changes to `lib/claude` or `lib/delivery` required.\n14\t\n15\t## Related Docs\n16\t\n17\t- [[agent-crd-specification.md]] — Config CRD fields\n18\t- [[agent-job-interface.md]] — Pattern B contract (env vars, Kafka, exit codes)\n19\t- [[agent-job-lifecycle.md]] — full task → job → result flow\n20\t- `agent/claude/README.md` — template agent README\n21\t\n22\t---\n23\t\n24\t## Architecture Recap\n25\t\n26\t```\n27\tObsidian task → task/controller → Kafka (agent-task-v1-event)\n28\t                                     ↓\n29\t                                  task/executor\n30\t                                     ↓ spawns K8s Job\n31\t                              agent-<domain> (your binary)\n32\t                                     ↓ spawns subprocess\n33\t                                  claude --print (Claude Code CLI)\n34\t                                     ↓ uses\n35\t                              scripts/*.sh + WebFetch + ...\n36\t                                     ↓\n37\t                         JSON result → lib/delivery → Kafka (agent-task-v1-request)\n38\t                                     ↓\n39\t                                task/controller → git writeback\n40\t```\n41\t\n42\tYour agent is the thin wrapper between the task pipeline and Claude Code. It:\n43\t1. Receives `TASK_CONTENT` from env\n44\t2. Assembles a prompt via `lib/claude` (embedded workflow.md + output-format.md + your domain prompts)\n45\t3. Spawns `claude --print --allowedTools=...` in a subprocess with a restricted env\n46\t4. Parses the stdout JSON result\n47\t5. Publishes it to Kafka via `lib/delivery.KafkaResultDeliverer`\n48\t\n49\t---\n50\t\n51\t## Step-by-Step: New Claude Agent\n52\t\n53\t### 1. Copy the template\n54\t\n55\t```bash\n56\tcp -r ~/Documents/workspaces/agent/agent/claude \\\n57\t      ~/Documents/workspaces/<your-repo>/agent/<domain>\n58\tcd ~/Documents/workspaces/<your-repo>/agent/<domain>\n59\t```\n60\t\n61\tRename module in `go.mod`, update imports in `main.go`, `pkg/`.\n62\t\n63\t### 2. Decide the tool surface\n64\t\n65\tPick the **minimum** `ALLOWED_TOOLS` for your domain. Use built-in Claude tools and/or constrained Bash scripts. Prefer scripts over bare `Bash`.\n66\t\n67\t| Task shape | Typical tools |\n68\t|---|---|\n69\t| Web research | `WebSearch,WebFetch,Read,Grep` |\n70\t| Vault I/O via git-rest | `Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-write.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Grep` |\n71\t| API query | `Bash(scripts/api-read.sh:*),Grep` |\n72\t| Code edits | `Read,Write,Edit,Grep,Glob,Bash(go:*),Bash(make:*)` |\n73\t| Hybrid (vault + API) | combine vault-*.sh + api-*.sh + `Grep` |\n74\t\n75\t**Rules of thumb:**\n76\t- Never grant bare `Bash` unless the task truly needs arbitrary shell\n77\t- Wrap every external I/O in a script under `agent/scripts/` so the allowlist stays `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`\n78\t- Exclude `Write` unless agent must produce a file (most agents return JSON via stdout)\n79\t\n80\t### 3. Write domain scripts\n81\t\n82\t`agent/scripts/*.sh` are your API surface to Claude. Keep them:\n83\t- Pure I/O — one purpose per script\n84\t- `set -e -o pipefail`\n85\t- Fail loudly if env vars missing (`: \"${VAR:?VAR is required}\"`)\n86\t- Treat stdout as the result, stderr for diagnostics\n87\t\n88\tPrecedent: `trading/agent/trade-analysis/agent/scripts/`:\n89\t- `trading-api-read.sh` — HTTP GET to trading API with optional basic auth\n90\t- `vault-read.sh`, `vault-write.sh`, `vault-list.sh` — curl to git-rest HTTP service\n91\t\n92\t### 4. Write domain prompts\n93\t\n94\tReplace `pkg/prompts/workflow.md` with your domain workflow. Keep `output-format.md` standard (JSON `{status, message, ...}`) — `lib/delivery` expects it.\n95\t\n96\tUse `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` for hard guardrails (no internal network, no secret exfiltration, no shell escapes, forbidden paths). Agent-claude's default CLAUDE.md is a good baseline — keep the Forbidden/Output/Tools/Data sections.\n97\t\n98\t### 5. Thread domain env through main.go\n99\t\n100\t**CRITICAL:** `lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,ZONEINFO,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL`). Any custom env your scripts need (API URLs, credentials) must be explicitly forwarded via `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env`:\n101\t\n102\t```go\n103\ttype application struct {\n104\t    // ... standard fields ...\n105\t    TradingAPIURL      string `required:\"true\"  arg:\"trading-api-url\"      env:\"TRADING_API_URL\"`\n106\t    TradingAPIUsername string `required:\"false\" arg:\"trading-api-username\" env:\"TRADING_API_USERNAME\" display:\"length\"`\n107\t    TradingAPIPassword string `required:\"false\" arg:\"trading-api-password\" env:\"TRADING_API_PASSWORD\" display:\"length\"`\n108\t}\n109\t\n110\tfunc (a *application) Run(ctx context.Context, sentryClient libsentry.Client) error {\n111\t    taskRunner := factory.CreateTaskRunner(\n112\t        a.ClaudeConfigDir, a.AgentDir,\n113\t        claudelib.AllowedTools{\n114\t            \"Grep\",\n115\t            \"Bash(scripts/trading-api-read.sh:*)\",\n116\t        },\n117\t        claudelib.SonnetClaudeModel,\n118\t        map[string]string{\n119\t            \"TRADING_API_URL\":      a.TradingAPIURL,\n120\t            \"TRADING_API_USERNAME\": a.TradingAPIUsername,\n121\t            \"TRADING_API_PASSWORD\": a.TradingAPIPassword,\n122\t        },\n123\t        // ...\n124\t    )\n125\t    // ...\n126\t}\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\t**Symptom of forgetting:** script fails with `X is required` even though `kubectl describe pod` shows the var is set. The pod has it — the Claude subprocess doesn't.\n130\t\n131\t**Precedent:** `trading/agent/trade-analysis` commit `1ccfa674cf` fixed exactly this.\n132\t\n133\tUse `display:\"length\"` on credential fields so startup logs show length only, not the secret.\n134\t\n135\t### 6. K8s manifests\n136\t\n137\tThree files under `agent/<domain>/k8s/`:\n138\t\n139\t**`agent-<domain>.yaml`** — the Config CRD. `spec.env` becomes pod env:\n140\t\n141\t```yaml\n142\tapiVersion: agent.benjamin-borbe.de/v1\n143\tkind: Config\n144\tmetadata:\n145\t  name: agent-<domain>\n146\t  namespace: '{{ \"NAMESPACE\" | env }}'\n147\tspec:\n148\t  assignee: <domain>-agent           # matches task assignee\n149\t  image: docker.quant.benjamin-borbe.de:443/agent-<domain>\n150\t  heartbeat: 5m\n151\t  secretName: agent-<domain>\n152\t  volumeClaim: agent-<domain>         # PVC with Claude Code OAuth config\n153\t  volumeMountPath: /home/claude/.claude\n154\t  env:\n155\t    ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Grep,Bash(scripts/trading-api-read.sh:*)\"\n156\t    TRADING_API_URL: http://frontend-gateway:9090\n157\t  resources:\n158\t    requests: {cpu: 500m, memory: 1Gi, ephemeral-storage: 2Gi}\n159\t    limits:   {cpu: 500m, memory: 1Gi, ephemeral-storage: 2Gi}\n160\t```\n161\t\n162\t**`agent-<domain>-secret.yaml`** — credentials via teamvault templating:\n163\t\n164\t```yaml\n165\tapiVersion: v1\n166\tkind: Secret\n167\ttype: Opaque\n168\tmetadata:\n169\t  name: agent-<domain>\n170\t  namespace: '{{ \"NAMESPACE\" | env }}'\n171\tdata:\n172\t  SENTRY_DSN:          '{{ \"SENTRY_DSN_KEY\"         | env | teamvaultUrl      | base64 }}'\n173\t  TRADING_API_USERNAME:'{{ \"FRONTEND_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"| env | teamvaultUser     | base64 }}'\n174\t  TRADING_API_PASSWORD:'{{ \"FRONTEND_GATEWAY_API_KEY\"| env | teamvaultPassword | base64 }}'\n175\t```\n176\t\n177\t**`agent-<domain>-pvc.yaml`** — PVC for Claude Code OAuth config (shared across runs, seeded once per `docs/claude-oauth-setup.md`).\n178\t\n179\t### 7. Build + deploy\n180\t\n181\tMakefile should include the standard BUCA chain (build → upload → commit → apply). Copy from `trading/agent/trade-analysis/Makefile`.\n182\t\n183\t```bash\n184\tcd agent/<domain>\n185\tBRANCH=dev make buca\n186\t```\n187\t\n188\t### 8. Register assignee → agent mapping\n189\t\n190\tEnsure `task/executor` CRDs are synced so a task with `assignee: <domain>-agent` routes to your image. The Config CRD handles this automatically once applied.\n191\t\n192\t### 9. Smoke test\n193\t\n194\tCreate a minimal task in OpenClaw vault:\n195\t\n196\t```markdown\n197\t---\n198\tassignee: <domain>-agent\n199\tstatus: in_progress\n200\tphase: in_progress\n201\ttask_identifier: <uuid>\n202\t---\n203\tTags: [[Task]]\n204\t\n205\t---\n206\t\n207\t<minimal domain task description>\n208\t```\n209\t\n210\tVerify end-to-end:\n211\t1. `kubectlquant -n dev get job -w` — job spawned\n212\t2. `kubectlquant -n dev logs job/<name>` — agent started, args printed include your domain fields\n213\t3. Task result appears in vault after agent exits\n214\t\n215\t**Common pitfalls:**\n216\t- Task content pollution from retries — create fresh task with new UUID between runs\n217\t- Image cache — confirm `:dev` image digest changed after `make buca`\n218\t- Allowlist gaps — check Claude's tool invocations in logs, grant missing tools explicitly\n219\t\n220\t---\n221\t\n222\t## Minimal Files Changed vs Template\n223\t\n224\tWhen forking `agent/claude`:\n225\t\n226\t| File | Change |\n227\t|---|---|\n228\t| `go.mod` | new module path |\n229\t| `main.go` | add domain env fields, thread into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` |\n230\t| `pkg/prompts/workflow.md` | domain workflow |\n231\t| `pkg/prompts/output-format.md` | usually unchanged |\n232\t| `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md` | domain guardrails |\n233\t| `agent/scripts/*.sh` | domain shell APIs |\n234\t| `k8s/agent-<domain>.yaml` | new CRD with `spec.env` |\n235\t| `k8s/agent-<domain>-secret.yaml` | teamvault wiring |\n236\t| `k8s/agent-<domain>-pvc.yaml` | PVC for OAuth config |\n237\t| `Dockerfile`, `Makefile` | rename image + module |\n238\t| `lib/claude`, `lib/delivery` | **never** — shared |\n239\t\n240\t---\n241\t\n242\t## Troubleshooting\n243\t\n244\t| Symptom | Cause | Fix |\n245\t|---|---|---|\n246\t| Script: `X is required` despite pod env set | `lib/claude` env allowlist | thread X via `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` |\n247\t| Job respawns after success | `current_job` not cleared by controller | known executor bug, separate fix |\n248\t| Claude refuses tool use | `ALLOWED_TOOLS` missing | add to CRD `spec.env`, redeploy |\n249\t| Task result stays \"in_progress\" | agent crashed before Kafka publish | check `kubectlquant logs` for panic |\n250\t| Image not updated after `make buca` | wrong branch or cache | `BRANCH=dev make buca` from correct worktree, confirm digest in registry |\n251\t\n252\t---\n253\t\n254\t## References\n255\t\n256\t- `lib/claude/claude-runner.go:93` — env allowlist source\n257\t- `lib/claude/allowed-tools.go` — tool allowlist parser\n258\t- `task/executor/pkg/spawner/job_spawner.go` — CRD `spec.env` → pod env\n259\t- `trading/agent/trade-analysis/` — complete Claude-based agent example\n260\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b28d6fdd9d31fe55","session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"602bffa8-03ed-4d10-95b0-b19dc383cc56","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:39:05.127Z","subagent_type":"dark-factory:prompt-auditor","task_description":"Audit prompt 1"}
