{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"acaa9700a6ada4e1b","tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cbee98593beadc5","status":"completed","output_file":"/tmp/claude-1000/-workspace/d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308/tasks/acaa9700a6ada4e1b.output","summary":"# Prompt Audit Report: Wire the diagnoser: dispatch, phase chain, README mapping and changelog\n\n**File**: `/workspace/prompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md`\n**Score**: 7/10\n**Status**: Good — one internal contradiction must be fixed; several minor accuracy items\n\n## DoD Checklist\n- [x] `<summary>` present and plain-language (8 bullets, no file paths / struct names / signatures)\n- [x] `<objective>` states end state (1 paragraph, what + why)\n- [x] `<context>` present (extensive, with verified-facts block and reviewer open questions)\n- [x] `<requirements>` numbered (0–10) and specific, with exact paths and signatures\n- [x] `<constraints>` present (contract, frozen rules, escalation mechanics, scope, no-knob)\n- [x] `<verification>` present with runnable container-executable commands\n- [x] All paths repo-relative (the only absolute paths are `/home/node/.claude/...`, the container's own mounted tooling — valid)\n- [x] No bare `git ` commands in `<verification>` (or anywhere in the file). Target repo runs `hideGit=true` (`.dark-factory.log`: `hideGit=true hideGitSource=arg`), but the prompt issues no `git` — no false-positive-pass risk\n- [x] No operator-only commands in `<verification>` (`docker`/`make buca`/`dark-factory`/`kubectl*`/`scripts/*.sh`/`gh pr` — none). AC10 is explicitly excluded from `<verification>` (line 64)\n- [x] File in `prompts/` inbox (not `prompts/in-progress/`)\n- [x] Filename `3-spec-002-...` uses the allowed single-digit ordering prefix; not a dark-factory global `NNN-` prefix\n- [x] Filename reflects the primary change (dispatch wiring + docs)\n- [x] Status is `draft` (valid)\n- [~] Frontmatter carries `branch`, which is not in the allowed inbox set (`spec`, `status`, `created`, `issue`). Minor — the completed spec-001 prompts also carry `branch`, so it appears tolerated (see Recommendations)\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed across the prompt set: the wiring prompt covers the \"pod dies between phases\" (AC3 j, entry at `ai_review`) and \"stale `## Failure` survives\" (AC3 a) rows directly; the rest are prompt 1/2 deliverables\n- [x] Security concerns from the spec reflected in `<constraints>` (no committed mapping data, heading rule, read-only allowlist, no pod-log reads)\n- [x] External calls: the prompt's own code crosses no external boundary; tests use `agentmocks.ClaudeRunner` (no HTTP/exec). The shared suite carries a 60 s timeout (`factory_suite_test.go:21`)\n- [x] New constant flows through a library validator **and is tested**: requirement 5 adds `Expect(factory.TaskTypeDefectDiagnose.Validate(ctx)).To(Succeed())` against `agentlib`'s `^[a-z0-9-]+$` / 63-char contract. Exemplary — this is exactly the level-1 contract test the DoD asks for\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>` (only a \"never `-mod=vendor`\" constraint, which is correct)\n- [x] No cross-repo writes\n- [x] Container-autonomous: no operator-only/runtime steps and no operator-vs-agent split. AC10's port-forwards/live run are explicitly fenced off (\"Do not attempt it and do not add it to `<verification>`\")\n- [x] Sibling entry points covered: `CreateAgentFromRunner` is edited, and **both** callers (`CreateAgent` — the local-CLI path — and `CreateAgentProvider` — the Kafka path) are updated by requirements 2 and 3; `cmd/run-task/main.go` and `main.go` keep compiling. The sibling-coverage check passes cleanly\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable pattern >10 lines (requirement 6 is test prose; requirements 1/3 are short snippets)\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>` (`docs/verdict-gate.md`, `docs/dod.md`, `scenarios/001-...`)\n- [x] Existing coding plugin docs referenced in `<context>` (testing, factory, error-wrapping, precommit, changelog guides)\n- [x] Domain knowledge (mapping form) is pointed at `docs/verdict-gate.md` and re-stated only as the README deliverable, not duplicated as a doc\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `const serviceName = \"defect-diagnoser-agent\"` | `pkg/factory/factory.go:26` | Correct |\n| `CreateAgent` / `CreateAgentFromRunner` / `CreateAgentProvider` signatures (all as quoted) | `pkg/factory/factory.go:90,107,133` | Correct |\n| \"exactly two call sites of `CreateAgentFromRunner`, both in `factory.go`\" | `pkg/factory/factory.go:98,142` | Correct |\n| `factory_test.go` asserts `[healthcheck llm oauth-probe]` and `TaskTypeLLM` returns the domain agent | `pkg/factory/factory_test.go:41,85` | Correct |\n| `agentlib.NewAgentProvider(name, map[TaskType]*Agent)`; miss message `unknown task_type %q for %s; accepted: %v`, sorted | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_agent-provider.go:30,54` | Correct |\n| `TaskType.Validate` regex `^[a-z0-9-]+$`, 63-char limit | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-type.go:15,35` | Correct |\n| `TaskTypeLLM=\"llm\"`, `TaskTypeHealthcheck=\"healthcheck\"`, deprecated `TaskTypeOAuthProbe=\"oauth-probe\"`; no `defect-diagnose` const | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-type.go:50,62,65` | Correct |\n| `healthcheck.NewAgent(step)` / `healthcheck.NewClaudeStep(runner)` | `agent@v0.89.0/healthcheck/healthcheck-agent.go:15`, `...-claude-step.go:23` | Correct |\n| `delivery.NewFileResultDeliverer(generator, filePath)`; `NewPassthroughContentGenerator()` applies status/phase + `## Failure` | `agent@v0.89.0/delivery/result-deliverer.go:46`, `content-generator.go:184` | Correct |\n| `agentmocks.ClaudeRunner` offers `RunReturns`/`RunReturnsOnCall`/`RunCallCount`/`RunArgsForCall` | `agent@v0.89.0/mocks/claude-claude-runner.go:50,62,69,79` | Correct |\n| `claudelib.AgentDir` is a string type; `Agent.Run(ctx, domain.TaskPhase, string, ResultDeliverer)`; `agentlib.NewPhase(name domain.TaskPhase, steps...)` | `claude/agent-dir.go:10`, `agent_agent.go:45`, `agent_phase.go:24` | Correct |\n| `domain.TaskPhasePlanning/Execution/AIReview` | `vault-cli@v0.126.3/pkg/domain/task_phase.go:16,22` | Correct |\n| `docs/verdict-gate.md` § The verdict block / § Service → repo mapping input / § Model-output heading rule | `docs/verdict-gate.md:5,26,36` | Correct |\n| README headings `### Config CRD env pattern` / `### Claude subprocess env allowlist`; CHANGELOG `## v0.0.0`; scenario 001 Setup `service_repo.` + Step 1 `defect_id` | `README.md:45,66`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `scenarios/001-...md` | Correct |\n\nEvery cited symbol, signature, file path, heading and line was verified against the module cache / repo. No stale references.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Factory zero business logic (`Create*` prefix, no conditional/loop) | `go-factory-pattern.md` | Compliant — requirement 1 mandates \"composition only: no conditional, no loop, no error path\" |\n| Error wrapping (`errors.Wrapf`, never `fmt.Errorf`) | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant — no `fmt.Errorf` inlined; guide referenced in `<context>` |\n| External test packages, Ginkgo/Gomega, `DescribeTable` | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant — `package factory_test`, existing suite reused, `DescribeTable` suggested |\n| Linter limits on test files (`funlen`, `dupl`, golines 100) | `go-precommit.md` | Compliant — requirement 6 explicitly requires factoring shared helpers to satisfy `dupl` |\n| Time injection (no deps created inside factory) | `go-time-injection.md` | Compliant — no time dependency added |\n| Test-only package-level mutable state (`var X` + `SetX`) | `go-composition.md` | Compliant — none introduced |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the behavior the prompt ships. The constraints explicitly *forbid* a confidence-threshold knob and a gate opt-out flag, matching the spec's Non-goals\n- [x] Every element is demanded by the spec: `TaskTypeDefectDiagnose` const + dispatch (DB1/AC2), phase-chain wiring (AC3), README mapping section (AC9), CHANGELOG bullet (AC9), the ten AC3 cases\n- [x] No future-proofing knobs; the only \"extra\" (the `Validate` boundary test) is a DoD requirement, not scope creep\n\n## Critical Issues\n\n### 1. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` is simultaneously forbidden in `pkg/factory/` and required in the new tests — the verification line cannot pass (or passes vacuously)\n\nThree requirements and one verification line disagree about the same string:\n\n- Requirement 3 (line 175): *\"The map has exactly three entries. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` must not appear anywhere in `pkg/factory/`.\"*\n- Requirement 4 (line 177): *\"Add one spec asserting `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` now misses with `unknown task_type`.\"*\n- Requirement 5 (line 183): *\"`Get(ctx, agentlib.TaskTypeLLM)` returns an error whose message contains `unknown task_type`.\"*\n- Verification (line 268): `! grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' pkg/factory/`\n\nThe two new test files (`pkg/factory/diagnoser_dispatch_test.go`, `pkg/factory/phase_chain_test.go`) and the edited `factory_test.go` all live **under `pkg/factory/`**, and requirements 4 and 5 instruct the executor to reference `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` in them. So the verification line's target directory contains the very string it forbids.\n\nI verified the grep semantics on this image: `grep` is **ugrep 7.8.4**, which searches a directory **recursively by default** even without `-r` — `grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' <dir>` exits 0 when a file beneath it matches. So the line evaluates to `! 0` → **fails**, making `<verification>` unpassable as written. On a GNU-grep image the same line errors on the directory (`Is a directory`, exit 2) → `! 2` → passes **for the wrong reason**, i.e. a false-positive verification pass that never actually enforced requirement 3. Either way the requirement as written is unsatisfiabl