ressing the exact `increment_frontmatter`-style failure the DoD's canonical example describes.\n  - **Failure-mode-driven details are pinned** — the `trigger_count: 1` / `max_triggers: 3` fixture rationale, the `RunReturns` default envelope to avoid nil-result panics, and the `dupl`-aware helper factoring are all thoughtful.\n  \n  ## Summary\n  This is a high-quality, deeply-researched prompt: all required sections are present, every code reference checks out, sibling entry points are covered, and it is fully container-autonomous. The single blocking defect is the `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` contradiction between requirement 3 / verification line 268 and requirements 4–5 — it either fails verification outright (ugrep recurses the directory) or produces a vacuous pass (GNU grep), so fix the grep scope and requirement 3's wording first. The CHANGELOG \"add an `## Unreleased` section\" wording and the \"two accepted-types assertions\" miscount are the next most valuable corrections.\nagentId: acaa9700a6ada4e1b (use SendMessage with to: 'acaa9700a6ada4e1b', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent)\n<usage>subagent_tokens: 125999\ntool_uses: 26\nduration_ms: 491379</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0a8f161-dbd4-4f10-88f7-931e909fc308","uuid":"87a56ae3-0899-4215-80e7-a8cbbd5de633","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:39:24.313Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Audit this dark-factory prompt file against the Prompt Definition of Done:\n\n`prompts/3-spec-002-wiring-dispatch-and-docs.md`\n\nIt was generated from the spec `specs/in-progress/002-diagnose-observed-defect-with-verdict-gate.md` and is the third of three prompts for that spec (the others are `prompts/1-spec-002-verdict-gate.md` and `prompts/2-spec-002-per-phase-prompts.md`). The spec's dependency `specs/in-progress/001-read-only-observation-toolkit.md` is being executed concurrently by the dark-factory daemon; its prompts are at `prompts/completed/001-spec-001-http-observation-