- [x] Filename reflects the primary change (dispatch wiring + docs)\n- [x] Status is `draft` (valid)\n- [~] Frontmatter carries `branch`, which is not in the allowed inbox set (`spec`, `status`, `created`, `issue`). Minor — the completed spec-001 prompts also carry `branch`, so it appears tolerated (see Recommendations)\n\n## Failure Mode Coverage\n- [x] Spec failure modes addressed across the prompt set: the wiring prompt covers the \"pod dies between phases\" (AC3 j, entry at `ai_review`) and \"stale `## Failure` survives\" (AC3 a) rows directly; the rest are prompt 1/2 deliverables\n- [x] Security concerns from the spec reflected in `<constraints>` (no committed mapping data, heading rule, read-only allowlist, no pod-log reads)\n- [x] External calls: the prompt's own code crosses no external boundary; tests use `agentmocks.ClaudeRunner` (no HTTP/exec). The shared suite carries a 60 s timeout (`factory_suite_test.go:21`)\n- [x] New constant flows through a library validator **and is tested**: requirement 5 adds `Expect(factory.TaskTypeDefectDiagnose.Validate(ctx)).To(Succeed())` against `agentlib`'s `^[a-z0-9-]+$` / 63-char contract. Exemplary — this is exactly the level-1 contract test the DoD asks for\n- [x] No `go mod vendor` in `<requirements>`/`<verification>` (only a \"never `-mod=vendor`\" constraint, which is correct)\n- [x] No cross-repo writes\n- [x] Container-autonomous: no operator-only/runtime steps and no operator-vs-agent split. AC10's port-forwards/live run are explicitly fenced off (\"Do not attempt it and do not add it to `<verification>`\")\n- [x] Sibling entry points covered: `CreateAgentFromRunner` is edited, and **both** callers (`CreateAgent` — the local-CLI path — and `CreateAgentProvider` — the Kafka path) are updated by requirements 2 and 3; `cmd/run-task/main.go` and `main.go` keep compiling. The sibling-coverage check passes cleanly\n\n## Documentation Placement\n- [x] No inlined reusable pattern >10 lines (requirement 6 is test prose; requirements 1/3 are short snippets)\n- [x] Existing project docs referenced in `<context>` (`docs/verdict-gate.md`, `docs/dod.md`, `scenarios/001-...`)\n- [x] Existing coding plugin docs referenced in `<context>` (testing, factory, error-wrapping, precommit, changelog guides)\n- [x] Domain knowledge (mapping form) is pointed at `docs/verdict-gate.md` and re-stated only as the README deliverable, not duplicated as a doc\n\n## Code Reference Verification\n| Reference | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| `const serviceName = \"defect-diagnoser-agent\"` | `pkg/factory/factory.go:26` | Correct |\n| `CreateAgent` / `CreateAgentFromRunner` / `CreateAgentProvider` signatures (all as quoted) | `pkg/factory/factory.go:90,107,133` | Correct |\n| \"exactly two call sites of `CreateAgentFromRunner`, both in `factory.go`\" | `pkg/factory/factory.go:98,142` | Correct |\n| `factory_test.go` asserts `[healthcheck llm oauth-probe]` and `TaskTypeLLM` returns the domain agent | `pkg/factory/factory_test.go:41,85` | Correct |\n| `agentlib.NewAgentProvider(name, map[TaskType]*Agent)`; miss message `unknown task_type %q for %s; accepted: %v`, sorted | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_agent-provider.go:30,54` | Correct |\n| `TaskType.Validate` regex `^[a-z0-9-]+$`, 63-char limit | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-type.go:15,35` | Correct |\n| `TaskTypeLLM=\"llm\"`, `TaskTypeHealthcheck=\"healthcheck\"`, deprecated `TaskTypeOAuthProbe=\"oauth-probe\"`; no `defect-diagnose` const | `agent@v0.89.0/agent_task-type.go:50,62,65` | Correct |\n| `healthcheck.NewAgent(step)` / `healthcheck.NewClaudeStep(runner)` | `agent@v0.89.0/healthcheck/healthcheck-agent.go:15`, `...-claude-step.go:23` | Correct |\n| `delivery.NewFileResultDeliverer(generator, filePath)`; `NewPassthroughContentGenerator()` applies status/phase + `## Failure` | `agent@v0.89.0/delivery/result-deliverer.go:46`, `content-generator.go:184` | Correct |\n| `agentmocks.ClaudeRunner` offers `RunReturns`/`RunReturnsOnCall`/`RunCallCount`/`RunArgsForCall` | `agent@v0.89.0/mocks/claude-claude-runner.go:50,62,69,79` | Correct |\n| `claudelib.AgentDir` is a string type; `Agent.Run(ctx, domain.TaskPhase, string, ResultDeliverer)`; `agentlib.NewPhase(name domain.TaskPhase, steps...)` | `claude/agent-dir.go:10`, `agent_agent.go:45`, `agent_phase.go:24` | Correct |\n| `domain.TaskPhasePlanning/Execution/AIReview` | `vault-cli@v0.126.3/pkg/domain/task_phase.go:16,22` | Correct |\n| `docs/verdict-gate.md` § The verdict block / § Service → repo mapping input / § Model-output heading rule | `docs/verdict-gate.md:5,26,36` | Correct |\n| README headings `### Config CRD env pattern` / `### Claude subprocess env allowlist`; CHANGELOG `## v0.0.0`; scenario 001 Setup `service_repo.` + Step 1 `defect_id` | `README.md:45,66`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `scenarios/001-...md` | Correct |\n\nEvery cited symbol, signature, file path, heading and line was verified against the module cache / repo. No stale references.\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Factory zero business logic (`Create*` prefix, no conditional/loop) | `go-factory-pattern.md` | Compliant — requirement 1 mandates \"composition only: no conditional, no loop, no error path\" |\n| Error wrapping (`errors.Wrapf`, never `fmt.Errorf`) | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant — no `fmt.Errorf` inlined; guide referenced in `<context>` |\n| External test packages, Ginkgo/Gomega, `DescribeTable` | `go-testing-guide.md` | Compliant — `package factory_test`, existing suite reused, `DescribeTable` suggested |\n| Linter limits on test files (`funlen`, `dupl`, golines 100) | `go-precommit.md` | Compliant — requirement 6 explicitly requires factoring shared helpers to satisfy `dupl` |\n| Time injection (no deps created inside factory) | `go-time-injection.md` | Compliant — no time dependency added |\n| Test-only package-level mutable state (`var X` + `SetX`) | `go-composition.md` | Compliant — none introduced |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the behavior the prompt ships. The constraints explicitly *forbid* a confidence-threshold knob and a gate opt-out flag, matching the spec's Non-goals\n- [x] Every element is demanded by the spec: `TaskTypeDefectDiagnose` const + dispatch (DB1/AC2), phase-chain wiring (AC3), README mapping section (AC9), CHANGELOG bullet (AC9), the ten AC3 cases\n- [x] No future-proofing knobs; the only \"extra\" (the `Validate` boundary test) is a DoD requirement, not scope creep\n\n## Critical Issues\n\n### 1. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` is simultaneously forbidden in `pkg/factory/` and required in the new tests — the verification line cannot pass (or passes vacuously)\n\nThree requirements and one verification line disagree about the same string:\n\n- Requirement 3 (line 175): *\"The map has exactly three entries. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` must not appear anywhere in `pkg/factory/`.\"*\n- Requirement 4 (line 177): *\"Add one spec asserting `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` now misses with `unknown task_type`.\"*\n- Requirement 5 (line 183): *\"`Get(ctx, agentlib.TaskTypeLLM)` returns an error whose message contains `unknown task_type`.\"*\n- Verification (line 268): `! grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' pkg/factory/`\n\nThe two new test files (`pkg/factory/diagnoser_dispatch_test.go`, `pkg/factory/phase_chain_test.go`) and the edited `factory_test.go` all live **under `pkg/factory/`**, and requirements 4 and 5 instruct the executor to reference `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` in them. So the verification line's target directory contains the very string it forbids.\n\nI verified the grep semantics on this image: `grep` is **ugrep 7.8.4**, which searches a directory **recursively by default** even without `-r` — `grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' <dir>` exits 0 when a file beneath it matches. So the line evaluates to `! 0` → **fails**, making `<verification>` unpassable as written. On a GNU-grep image the same line errors on the directory (`Is a directory`, exit 2) → `! 2` → passes **for the wrong reason**, i.e. a false-positive verification pass that never actually enforced requirement 3. Either way the requirement as written is unsatisfiable (the required tests necessarily contain the constant).\n\n**Fix — find/replace (scope requirement 3 and the grep to the production file):**\n\n- In requirement 3, replace verbatim:\n  > The map has exactly three entries. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` must not appear anywhere in `pkg/factory/`.\n  \n  with:\n  > The map has exactly three entries. `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` must not appear in `pkg/factory/factory.go` (the new tests reference it deliberately, to assert it is now rejected).\n\n- In `<verification>`, replace verbatim the line:\n  ```\n  ! grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' pkg/factory/\n  ```\n  with:\n  ```\n  ! grep -q 'agentlib.TaskTypeLLM' pkg/factory/factory.go\n  ```\n\n- While doing so, update the now-stale doc comment: `pkg/factory/factory.go:126-132` still says *\"TaskTypeLLM routes to the existing 3-phase domain agent.\"* Add a requirement bullet to rewrite that comment for the new table.\n\n**Alternative fix** (if the author prefers to keep requirement 3's \"anywhere in `pkg/factory/`\" wording): reword requirements 4 and 5 to use the literal `agentlib.TaskType(\"llm\")` instead of the `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` constant. The spec's own AC2 writes `Get(\"llm\")`, so this is faithful; it keeps the grep meaningful and lets it pass.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Requirement 8 is factually wrong about the file state.** `CHANGELOG.md` already has an `## Unreleased` section (two bullets from spec 001). \"Add an `## Unreleased` section above `## v0.0.0` with exactly one bullet\" can be read as *replace it with one bullet*, which would silently delete two shipped entries — and the verification grep (`sed -n '/^## Unreleased/,/^## v/p' | grep -ci 'diagnos'`) cannot detect that loss. Find/replace:\n   - OLD: `Add an `## Unreleased` section above `## v0.0.0` with exactly one bullet describing what was implemented.`\n   - NEW: `Append exactly one bullet to the existing `## Unreleased` section (do not replace the section or its existing bullets).`\n   Also fix `<context>` line 42 (\"the file to append an `## Unreleased` section to\" → \"the file whose `## Unreleased` section you append one bullet to\").\n\n2. **Requirement 4 miscounts the specs that change.** It says *\"the ones asserting `TaskTypeLLM` returns the domain agent and the two asserting the accepted-types list.\"* `pkg/factory/factory_test.go` has exactly **one** accepted-types assertion (line 84-86: `[healthcheck llm oauth-probe]`), not two. Find/replace: `the two asserting the accepted-types list` → `the one asserting the accepted-types list`.\n\n3. **Requirement 6 drops the spec's two-prompt assertion for cases (e) and (f).** Spec AC3's preamble requires that cases **(b), (d), (e) and (f)** all assert *\"the fake runner captured exactly two prompts, the second containing `scripts/prometheus-query.sh`.\"* Requirement 6 states this only for (b) and (d) (lines 201, 203); (e) and (f) (lines 204-205) assert only `phase: execution`. Add the two-prompt assertion to (e) and (f) to match the spec (the prompt's own open-question note 3 already claims all four do).\n\n4. **`agentDir` is joined unresolved while the runner resolves it.** Requirement 1 uses `filepath.Join(string(agentDir), \"repos\")`, but `claude-runner.go:170-173` calls `AgentDir.Resolve` (tilde expansion) before using it as the working directory. A `~`-prefixed `-agent-dir` would give the gate a literal-tilde clone root that never matches where `repo-clone.sh` actually wrote. The default (`\"agent\"`, relative to cwd) and the rung-1 operator run (`$(pwd)/agent`) are fine, so this is latent, not active. Suggest adding a sentence to requirement 1: \"`-agent-dir` is passed to the runner as-is; document that it must be an absolute or cwd-relative path (no `~`), because the gate joins it without tilde expansion.\"\n\n5. **Frontmatter carries `branch`.** The inbox frontmatter has `status`, `spec`, `created`, **`branch`**; the DoD's inbox set is `spec`, `status`, `created`, `issue`. The completed spec-001 prompts also carry `branch`, so this is likely generator/dark-factory behavior rather than an author error — flagging only for completeness.\n\n6. **State the new package's import path in requirement 1.** `verdict.NewGate(...)` is used without naming `github.com/bborbe/defect-diagnoser-agent/pkg/verdict`. It is inferable from prompt 1's deliverable, but the DoD prefers explicit import paths. Low priority.\n\n## Strengths\n- **Every code reference is accurate.** All signatures (`CreateAgentFromRunner`, `NewAgentProvider`, `Agent.Run`, `NewPhase`, `healthcheck.NewAgent`/`NewClaudeStep`, `NewFileResultDeliverer`, the `agentmocks` API), the two-call-site claim, the sorted accepted-types list, the `Validate` regex, and the doc/heading anchors were verified against the module cache and repo — no stale references found.\n- **Sibling entry points are handled explicitly.** The local-CLI path (`CreateAgent`) and the Kafka path (`CreateAgentProvider`) are both updated; the untouched callers (`cmd/run-task/main.go`, `main.go`) are called out as must-keep-compiling. This is the exact class the sibling-coverage rule targets, done right.\n- **Container-autonomy is clean and self-aware** — AC10's port-forwards/live run are fenced off with an explicit \"do not add to `<verification>`\".\n- **The boundary-crossing contract test is present** (`TaskTypeDefectDiagnose.Validate(ctx)`), addressing the exact `increment_frontmatter`-style failure the DoD's canonical example describes.\n- **Failure-mode-driven details are pinned** — the `trigger_count: 1` / `max_triggers: 3` fixture rationale, the `RunReturns` default envelope to avoid nil-result panics, and the `dupl`-aware helper factoring are all thoughtful.\n\n## Summary\nThis is a high-quality, deeply-researched prompt: all required sections are present, every code reference checks out, sibling entry points are covered, and it is fully container-autonomous. The single blocking defect is the `agentlib.TaskTypeLLM` contradiction between requirement 3 / verification line 268 and requirements 4–5 — it either fails verification outright (ugrep recurses the directory) or produces a vacuous pass (GNU grep), so fix the grep scope and requirement 3's wording first. The CHANGELOG \"add an `## Unreleased` section\" wording and the \"two accepted-types assertions\" miscount are the next most valuable corrections."}],"resolvedModel":"deepseek-v4-flash-max[1m]","totalDurationMs":491379,"totalTokens":125999,"totalToolUseCount":26,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"input_tokens":63,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":116992,"output_tokens":8432,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":10,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":16,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
