tter map[string]interface{}`; `String(key) (string, bool)` | `agent_task-frontmatter.go:16,144` | Correct |\n| `claude.NewAgentStep(claude.AgentStepConfig{Name,Runner,Instructions,EnvContext,OutputSection,NextPhase})`; `ReplaceSection` on done; no section on needs_input/failed | `claude/agent-step.go:56,25,205` | Correct |\n| `Agent.Run` in-process phase walk | `agent_agent.go:45` | Correct |\n| `delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator()`; writes `## Failure` from `result.Message` in a fence | `delivery/content-generator.go:184,136` | Correct |\n| `AgentResultInfo{Status,Output,Message,NextPhase,ContinueToNext,AgentTurns,InteractionCount}` | `agent_status.go:33` | Correct |\n| `agentmocks \"github.com/bborbe/agent/mocks\"` fake `ClaudeRunner` with `RunReturns`/`RunReturnsOnCall`/`RunCallCount`/`RunArgsForCall` | `mocks/claude-claude-runner.go` | Correct |\n| `errors.Errorf(ctx, …)` whose `Error()` == `fmt.Sprintf(...)`; `errors.Wrapf(ctx, err, …)` | `errors@v1.6.1/errors_new.go:17`, `errors_data-error.go:45` | Correct (`dataError.Error()` returns `d.err.Error()`) |\n| `domain.TaskPhasePlanning/Execution/AIReview` | `vault-cli@v0.126.3/pkg/domain/task_phase.go:22,25,31` | Correct |\n| `pkg/factory/factory.go`, `factory_test.go`, `factory_suite_test.go` | repo | Exist; `CreateAgentFromRunner` seam present |\n| `pkg/prompts/prompts.go`, `agent/.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `docs/dod.md`, `docs/verdict-gate.md`, `specs/in-progress/001-...`, `prompts/completed/001-spec-001-http-observation-scripts.md` | repo | All exist |\n| `$(go env GOMODCACHE)/github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0` | GOMODCACHE=`/home/node/go/pkg/mod` | Correct; matches `go.mod` `github.com/bborbe/agent v0.89.0` |\n\n## Coding Guidelines Compliance\n\n| Guideline | File | Status |\n|-----------|------|--------|\n| Error wrapping uses `errors.Wrapf`/`errors.Errorf`, never `fmt.Errorf` | `go-error-wrapping-guide.md` | Compliant (req 4 explicitly; verification enforces `! grep 'fmt\\.Errorf'`) |\n| Constructor returns interface, not struct | `go-patterns.md` (line 14) / container CLAUDE.md self-review | **Deviation (documented)** — `NewGate(...) *Gate` (req 2). The prompt flags it as open question #7 with a sound rationale (no fake, no second impl). See R6. |\n| No new interface with no consumer; `make generate` untouched | `go-composition.md` | Compliant (req 2 forbids a new interface; no `//counterfeiter:generate`; repo has only `main_test.go`'s `//go:generate`) |\n| Test-only package-level mutable state (`var X` + `SetX()`) | `go-composition.md` § Anti-Pattern | Compliant — `VerdictFieldOrder` is production data consumed by the extraction, with no setter |\n| Context propagation (`ctx` threaded, no `context.Background()` in `pkg/`) | `go-patterns.md` | Compliant |\n| License header on new `.go` files | `go-precommit.md` / `go-licensing-guide.md` | Not specified (R9) — `make precommit`'s `addlicense` target auto-adds it, so non-fatal |\n\n## YAGNI Pass (scope-creep detector)\n\n- [x] No opt-out flag for the shipped behavior — `<constraints>` explicitly forbids a gate opt-out flag and a confidence-threshold knob (spec Non-goal).\n- [x] Every branch/constant is demanded by the spec: rules a–k and the pinned reason strings come from `docs/verdict-gate.md` / AC4–AC7; `parseOutcome`'s three failure values map 1:1 to rule a's three pinned messages; `NewGate`'s two params (`envContext`, `cloneRoot`) are both consumed (rule h / line guard).\n- [x] No \"future-proofing\" knobs. `Gate` is concrete precisely to *avoid* dead surface.\n\n**No YAGNI hits.**\n\n## Critical Issues\n\nNone. All Critical-class checks pass: no hideGit-violating `git` commands (confirmed `hideGit=true` is active), no operator-only commands in `<verification>`, no cross-repo writes, no `go mod vendor`, fully container-autonomous, boundary contract tests present, sibling entry points symmetric, and every code reference verified against the actual module source.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n**R1 — Inconsistent `dupl` claim (line 343).** `.golangci.yml` excludes `dupl` for test files (`- linters: [dupl] path: \"_test\\\\.go$\"`), so `dupl` does **not** analyse `_test.go`.\n- OLD: `` reuse them everywhere; factor them into helpers so no `It` body is a copy of another (`dupl` is enabled and analyses test files). ``\n- NEW: `` reuse them everywhere; factor them into helpers so no `It` body is a copy of another (`funlen`, `gocognit` and `nestif` do apply to test files; `dupl` is excluded for `_test.go` in `.golangci.yml`, but factor the fixtures anyway so the tables stay readable). ``\n\n**R2 — Pinned reason strings are not on the \"authoritative\" page.** `docs/verdict-gate.md` contains `no line cited; evidence:`, `evidence cites no live read`, `service %q does not resolve`, the three line-guard reasons and the heading-rule message, but **none** of `verdict section missing`, `verdict yaml block missing`, `verdict yaml does not parse`, `field %q contains a newline`, `confidence %q is not one of High, Medium, Low`, `field %q is missing or empty`, `file:line is not a repo-relative <path>:<positive line>`, `defect_id mismatch: verdict %q, frontmatter %q`, `repo %q does not match mapped repo %q`. The prompt's claim at line 36 (\"Its rules, reason strings and quoting rules are reproduced verbatim\") and line 117 (\"verbatim from `docs/verdict-gate.md`\") overstates this. Since the prompt also says \"A rule change updates that page in the same change\", the page should carry the exact strings or the prompt should name them as prompt-authored.\n- OLD (line 36): `` Its rules, reason strings and quoting rules are reproduced verbatim in `<requirements>` below so you do not have to trust a grep. ``\n- NEW: `` Its rules and quoting rules are reproduced verbatim in `<requirements>` below, and the exact per-rule message formats are pinned there too (rules a, b, d, e, g and i have no exact format on the docs page — the pinned table below is the source for those strings). ``\n\n**R3 — Internal contradiction: `<constraints>` vs requirements 7/9 on `service_repo.` in tests (line 428).** The constraint says \"Do NOT add any `service_repo.` mapping entry to this repo's Config, code, **tests** or docs … no key/value pair may be hard-coded\", but requirement 7 mandates the test fixture `{\"service_repo.checkout\": \"bborbe/foo\"}` and requirement 9 the key `service_repo.agent-task-controller` (spec AC5 requires them). Prompt 3 has the explicit carve-out; prompt 1 does not. Align it:\n- OLD (line 428): `` - **Do NOT add any `service_repo.` mapping entry** to this repo's Config, code, tests or docs. The mapping is operator-supplied input delivered through `ENV_CONTEXT`. The literal prefix `\"service_repo.\"` exists in `pkg/verdict` only as the lookup prefix for the keys the operator supplies — it is not a mapping entry, and no key/value pair may be hard-coded. ``\n- NEW: `` - **Do NOT commit any `service_repo.` mapping entry** to this repo's Config, non-test code, or docs. The mapping is operator-supplied input delivered through `ENV_CONTEXT`. The literal prefix `\"service_repo.\"` exists in `pkg/verdict` only as the lookup prefix for the keys the operator supplies — it is not a mapping entry, and no key/value pair may be hard-coded. The one exception is the fixtures in requirements 7 and 9, which construct `service_repo.<service>` keys in their own local `envContext` to exercise rules h and i — that is simulated operator input, not committed mapping data. ``\n\n**R4 — Over-broad negative grep (line 468).** `! grep -rn 'agent/repos' pkg/verdict/` also matches explanatory comments, and requirement 11 (line 394) itself uses the literal `agent/repos/`; an agent that documents why it avoids that path fails its own verification.\n- OLD (line 394): `` Build the clone with `t.TempDir()` / `os.MkdirAll` and `os.WriteFile` — **never** under `agent/repos/`, which a sibling spec's tests own and which two concurrent runs would corrupt. ``\n- NEW: `` Build the clone with `t.TempDir()` / `os.MkdirAll` and `os.WriteFile` — **never** under `<agent dir>/repos/`, which a sibling spec's tests own and which two concurrent runs would corrupt. ``\n(and optionally add a positive assertion `grep -qF 't.TempDir()' pkg/verdict/lineguard_test.go` alongside line 468)\n\n**R5 — AC5's heading-injection row is under-asserted (line 377).** Requirement 9's heading-injection-through-evidence row asserts only the gate message + `PrefixMessage` safety, but AC5 additionally requires the *written task* assertions (the set of column-0 `#` lines, the column-0 fence lines). Route that row through the real content generator the way requirement 10 (line 392) does.\n- OLD (line 377): `` **Heading injection through evidence.** Rule c with an `evidence` whose value contains a line `## Verdict` and a line of three backticks. The gate's message quotes the evidence raw, and after `PrefixMessage` no line of the message starts with `#` and no line is a bare fence. Assert both. ``\n- NEW: `` **Heading injection through evidence.** Rule c with an `evidence` whose value contains a line `## Verdict` and a line of three backticks. The gate's message quotes the evidence raw, and after `PrefixMessage` no line of the message starts with `#` and no line is a bare fence. Then run the result through the real `delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator()` and assert the written task has `grep -c '^## Verdict'` = 0 and no injected column-0 `#` or fence line (AC5). ``\n\n**R6 — `NewGate` returns a concrete `*Gate` (lines 249, 274).** This deviates from `go-patterns.md`'s \"Constructor returns interface, not struct\" and the container self-review checklist. The prompt documents the rationale and raises it as open question #7, so it is defensible — but the reviewer must actually decide it before approve. If the reviewer requires the convention: change `func NewGate(...) *Gate` to `func NewGate(...) Gate` with a `//counterfeiter:generate`-annotated `Gate` interface + a `mocks/verdict-gate.go` fake, and update `NewExecutionStep`/`NewAIReviewStep` to accept `Gate`. (No change needed if the reviewer accepts the documented deviation.)\n\n**R7 — `branch:` in inbox frontmatter (line 5).** Not in the allowed inbox set (`spec`, `status`, `created`, `issue`). The archived prompt also carries it, so it is most likely daemon-stamped — if it was not, remove the line.\n\n**R8 — Consider referencing `docs/creating-claude-agents.md`** in `<context>`, or state why not. Low priority: it covers the fork/deploy layer and references stale paths (`lib/claude`, `agent/claude`, `make buca`) that this repo does not use.\n\n**R9 — State the BSD license header requirement for the new `.go` files** in requirement 1. `make precommit`'s `addlicense` target will add it automatically, but every existing file carries it, so naming it makes the diff deterministic.\n\n## Strengths\n\n- **Every framework symbol is real and verified.** I checked each claim in `<context>` (line 50–59) against `github.com/bborbe/agent@v0.89.0` in the module cache: `Step`, `Result`, `Markdown`/`Section`/`FindSection` (and the correct assertion that there is **no** `RemoveSection`), `TaskFrontmatter.String`, `claude.AgentStepConfig` field list, the `ReplaceSection`-on-done / no-section-on-envelope behavior, `Agent.Run`, `AgentResultInfo`'s seven fields, `NewPassthroughContentGenerator`, the `agentmocks.ClaudeRunner` methods, and the `errors.Errorf`→`Error()` identity (verified via `dataError.Error()`). Zero hallucinated symbols. This is exactly what the prompt-generation rules demand.\n- **Boundary-crossing contract tests are exemplary.** Requirement 11 builds a real throwaway clone with `t.TempDir()`, exercises symlink-escape on both a file and a parent directory, and asserts the escaping sentinel file is untouched; requirement 10 drives the model-passthrough messages through the real `delivery.NewPassthroughContentGenerator()` and asserts on the delivered body including the `## Failure` fence. The heading-injection tests (req 9/10/12) cover the exact failure mode the framework's fence-ignoring splitter creates.\n- **Correctly container-scoped.** No operator steps, no `git`, no cluster commands; the operator rung (`AC10`) is deliberately excluded (and prompt 3 says so explicitly).\n- **YAGNI-disciplined.** The prompt pre-empts the exact scope-creep the DoD warns about (no gate opt-out flag, no confidence threshold), and every constant/branch traces to the spec.\n- **Pinned API + pinned reason strings** make the deliverable mechanically verifiable and keep prompt 1 / prompt 3 consistent (`NewGate(envContext, cloneRoot)`, `NewExecutionStep(inner, gate)`).\n- **`hideGit=true` is handled correctly by omission** — the prompt's verification is pure filesystem/build assertions, so the false-positive-pass failure mode cannot occur.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a high-quality, meticulously researched prompt: all six required sections are present, all framework and repo code references verify against the actual sources, and the container-autonomy / hideGit / cross-repo / vendor / boundary-test checks all pass with no Critical findings. The issues are minor but real: an internal contradiction between the `<constraints>` and requirements 7/9 over test-local `service_repo.` keys (R3), an over-broad verification grep that can false-positive on its own requirements text (R4), an inaccurate `dupl` claim (R1), and a documentation-completeness gap where the \"authoritative rule set\" page lacks most of the pinned reason strings the prompt calls verbatim (R2). **Priority action: fix R3 (align the constraint wording with prompt 3's test carve-out) and R4 (reword `agent/repos/` to `<agent dir>/repos/`), then decide open question #7 (R6) before approving.**"}],"resolvedModel":"deepseek-v4-flash-max[1m]","totalDurationMs":579521,"totalTokens":124575,"totalToolUseCount":29,"usage":{"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"input_tokens":105,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3200,"cache_read_input_tokens":